</figure>
<figure id="A4.F20" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2509.19702v1/x3.svg" id="A4.F20.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_figure_panel ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:286/13;" width="286" height="13"></object></div><div class="ltx_flex_break"></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_3"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2509.19702v1/ab_noise_0.01.svg" id="A4.F20.g2" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_figure_panel ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:143/109;" width="143" height="109"></object></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_3"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2509.19702v1/ab_noise_0.01_distr.svg" id="A4.F20.g3" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_figure_panel ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:143/111;" width="143" height="111"></object></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_3"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2509.19702v1/ab_noise_0.01_sto.svg" id="A4.F20.g4" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_figure_panel ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:143/111;" width="143" height="111"></object></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A4.F20.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 20</span>: </span><span id="A4.F20.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Performance with i.i.d. Gaussian noise (standard deviation <math id="A4.F20.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma=0.01" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.01</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma=0.01</annotation></semantics></math>) in the unconstrained (left), distributed (center) and stochastic data access (right) settings.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="A4.F21" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2509.19702v1/ab_sens_scale.svg" id="A4.F21.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_figure_panel ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:191/138;" width="191" height="138"></object></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2509.19702v1/ab_sens_ratio.svg" id="A4.F21.g2" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_figure_panel ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:191/138;" width="191" height="138"></object></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A4.F21.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 21</span>: </span><span id="A4.F21.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Best performance of EAGLE in 200 iterations as the step sizes are varied. Left: <math id="A4.F21.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.F21.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta</annotation></semantics></math> are both scaled by a common factor. Right: <math id="A4.F21.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math> is scaled by <math id="A4.F21.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sqrt{\text{ratio}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msqrt><mtext>ratio</mtext></msqrt><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sqrt{\text{ratio}}</annotation></semantics></math> while <math id="A4.F21.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta</annotation></semantics></math> is scaled by <math id="A4.F21.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1/\sqrt{\text{ratio}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><msqrt><mtext>ratio</mtext></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1/\sqrt{\text{ratio}}</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="A4.F21.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma/\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma/\eta</annotation></semantics></math> is scaled by <math id="A4.F21.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{ratio}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ratio</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{ratio}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<section id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Data distribution.</h4>

<div id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We perform ablations on various real-world data settings. As in the main body, we place ourselvels in the setting <math id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=d=240" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>240</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=d=240</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n^{\prime}=d^{\prime}=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n^{\prime}=d^{\prime}=2</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r=240" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>240</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r=240</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
<dl id="A4.I1" class="ltx_description" style="--ltx-enum-leftmargin:0cm;">
<dt id="A4.I1.ix1" class="ltx_item"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A4.I1.ix1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">SVD construction</span>.</span></dt>
<dd class="ltx_item">
<div id="A4.I1.ix1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.I1.ix1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Sample
<math id="A4.I1.ix1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{ij},B_{ij}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{ij},B_{ij}</annotation></semantics></math> orthogonal and set
<math id="A4.I1.ix1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z=A\Sigma B^{\top}/\sqrt{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>B</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>/</mo><msqrt><mi>r</mi></msqrt></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z=A\Sigma B^{\top}/\sqrt{r}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A4.I1.ix1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma</annotation></semantics></math> diagonal with entries log-uniform in <math id="A4.I1.ix1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[1e-2,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[1e-2,1]</annotation></semantics></math>.
This is the reference distribution in the simulation part.</p>
</div></dd>
<dt id="A4.I1.ix2" class="ltx_item"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A4.I1.ix2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Gaussian</span>.</span></dt>
<dd class="ltx_item">
<div id="A4.I1.ix2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.I1.ix2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Sample
<math id="A4.I1.ix2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{ij},B_{ij}\sim\mathcal{N}(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{ij},B_{ij}\sim\mathcal{N}(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math> and set
<math id="A4.I1.ix2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z=AB^{\top}/\sqrt{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>B</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>/</mo><msqrt><mi>r</mi></msqrt></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z=AB^{\top}/\sqrt{r}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Gaussian data is a widely made modeling assumption, and this is the distribution the transformer was trained on.</p>
</div></dd>
<dt id="A4.I1.ix3" class="ltx_item"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A4.I1.ix3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Student–<math id="A4.I1.ix3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{\nu}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>ν</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{\nu}</annotation></semantics></math> factors</span>.</span></dt>
<dd class="ltx_item">
<div id="A4.I1.ix3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.I1.ix3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Sample
<math id="A4.I1.ix3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{ij},B_{ij}\sim t_{\nu}/\!\sqrt{\nu/(\nu-2)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>ν</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.052em">/</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{ij},B_{ij}\sim t_{\nu}/\!\sqrt{\nu/(\nu-2)}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A4.I1.ix3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu=4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu=4</annotation></semantics></math> and set
<math id="A4.I1.ix3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z=AB^{\top}/\sqrt{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>B</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>/</mo><msqrt><mi>r</mi></msqrt></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z=AB^{\top}/\sqrt{r}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Heavy-tailed entries create sporadic outliers, checking that the solver is
stable beyond sub-Gaussian data.</p>
</div></dd>
<dt id="A4.I1.ix4" class="ltx_item"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A4.I1.ix4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Correlated Gaussian factors</span>.</span></dt>
<dd class="ltx_item">
<div id="A4.I1.ix4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.I1.ix4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Draw each column of <math id="A4.I1.ix4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.I1.ix4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math>
from <math id="A4.I1.ix4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{N}(0,\Sigma)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{N}(0,\Sigma)</annotation></semantics></math> with
<math id="A4.I1.ix4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{ij}=\rho^{|i-j|}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{ij}=\rho^{|i-j|}</annotation></semantics></math> (<math id="A4.I1.ix4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho=0.8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.8</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho=0.8</annotation></semantics></math>).
Strong row/column correlations are typical in spatio-temporal panels and
challenge methods assuming independent observations.</p>
</div></dd>
<dt id="A4.I1.ix5" class="ltx_item"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A4.I1.ix5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Sparse Rademacher factors</span>.</span></dt>
<dd class="ltx_item">
<div id="A4.I1.ix5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.I1.ix5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">With sparsity <math id="A4.I1.ix5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p=0.1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p=0.1</annotation></semantics></math>, take
<math id="A4.I1.ix5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{ij}=s_{ij}\xi_{ij}/\sqrt{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>/</mo><msqrt><mi>p</mi></msqrt></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{ij}=s_{ij}\xi_{ij}/\sqrt{p}</annotation></semantics></math> where
<math id="A4.I1.ix5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\xi_{ij}\sim\mathrm{Bernoulli}(p)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>Bernoulli</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\xi_{ij}\sim\mathrm{Bernoulli}(p)</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A4.I1.ix5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{ij}\in\{\pm 1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo>±</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{ij}\in\{\pm 1\}</annotation></semantics></math> (analogous for
<math id="A4.I1.ix5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math>), then <math id="A4.I1.ix5.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z=AB^{\top}/\sqrt{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>B</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>/</mo><msqrt><mi>r</mi></msqrt></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z=AB^{\top}/\sqrt{r}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Entry-wise sparsity yields highly <em id="A4.I1.ix5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">coherent</em> singular vectors—a
worst-case regime for many theoretical guarantees.</p>
</div></dd>
<dt id="A4.I1.ix6" class="ltx_item"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A4.I1.ix6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Block / clustered factors</span>.</span></dt>
<dd class="ltx_item">
<div id="A4.I1.ix6.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.I1.ix6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Assign each of the <math id="A4.I1.ix6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math> rows to one
of <math id="A4.I1.ix6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> clusters (<math id="A4.I1.ix6.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=5</annotation></semantics></math>),
<math id="A4.I1.ix6.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A\in\{0,1\}^{d\times k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A\in\{0,1\}^{d\times k}</annotation></semantics></math> is one-hot, and
<math id="A4.I1.ix6.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B\in\mathbb{R}^{\,n\times k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B\in\mathbb{R}^{\,n\times k}</annotation></semantics></math> holds cluster centroids; set
<math id="A4.I1.ix6.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z=AB^{\top}/\sqrt{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>B</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>/</mo><msqrt><mi>k</mi></msqrt></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z=AB^{\top}/\sqrt{k}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Produces piece-wise-constant structure seen in recommender systems,
violating global incoherence yet preserving low rank.</p>
</div></dd>
</dl>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Larger systems.</h4>

<div id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We increase the size of the data matrix <math id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=d=1920" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1920</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=d=1920</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n^{\prime}=d^{\prime}=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n^{\prime}=d^{\prime}=2</annotation></semantics></math>; results are shown in Figure <a href="#A4.F19" title="Figure 19 ‣ D.3 Ablations for EAGLE ‣ Appendix D Further Details on Evaluation of EAGLE ‣ Linear Transformers Implicitly DiscoverUnified Numerical Algorithms" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">19</span></a>. These experiments further reveal that the Conjugate Gradient method does not converge reliably when applied to low-rank matrices. As a result, its performance is omitted from the main results in the low-rank setting.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Data noise.</h4>

<div id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To assess robustness to noise, we add moderate i.i.d. Gaussian noise to the matrix <math id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> and evaluate EAGLE in all three computational settings; results are presented in Figure <a href="#A4.F20" title="Figure 20 ‣ D.3 Ablations for EAGLE ‣ Appendix D Further Details on Evaluation of EAGLE ‣ Linear Transformers Implicitly DiscoverUnified Numerical Algorithms" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">20</span></a>. We observe that EAGLE exhibits the same form of implicit regularization during early iterations that is well-documented for gradient descent. Across all settings, EAGLE with early stopping achieves performance comparable to gradient descent, recovering regularized solutions that are more stable than the Nyström solution Additionally, we note that the addition of Gaussian noise to <math id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> inadvertently improves the conditioning of the matrix <math id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>, effectively reducing <math id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa(A)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa(A)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Sensitivity to step sizes.</h4>

<div id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To evaluate the sensitivity of EAGLE to the choice of step sizes, we conduct a series of controlled experiments in the unconstrained setting, using a small-scale configuration with <math id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=d=15" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>15</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=d=15</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n^{\prime}=d^{\prime}=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n^{\prime}=d^{\prime}=2</annotation></semantics></math>, and rank 15.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">First, we scale both step sizes <math id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta</annotation></semantics></math> by a common factor, as shown in Figure <a href="#A4.F21" title="Figure 21 ‣ D.3 Ablations for EAGLE ‣ Appendix D Further Details on Evaluation of EAGLE ‣ Linear Transformers Implicitly DiscoverUnified Numerical Algorithms" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">21</span></a> (left). This setup models scenarios in which the estimate of the scaling parameter <math id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{\ell}=1/\|A_{\ell}\|_{2}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{\ell}=1/\|A_{\ell}\|_{2}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> is inaccurate. The results indicate that scaling <math id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta</annotation></semantics></math> jointly by a factor in the range <math id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0.2,2]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0.2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0.2,2]</annotation></semantics></math> has minimal effect on performance.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Second, we vary the ratio <math id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma/\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma/\eta</annotation></semantics></math> to test the algorithm’s robustness to discrepancies between these two parameters, as illustrated in Figure <a href="#A4.F21" title="Figure 21 ‣ D.3 Ablations for EAGLE ‣ Appendix D Further Details on Evaluation of EAGLE ‣ Linear Transformers Implicitly DiscoverUnified Numerical Algorithms" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">21</span></a> (right). We find that EAGLE remains stable over a wide range of ratios; specifically, varying <math id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma/\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma/\eta</annotation></semantics></math> within <math id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0.2,2]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0.2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0.2,2]</annotation></semantics></math> has little impact on overall performance.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A5" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix E </span>Theoretical Analyses</h2>

<section id="A5.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">E.1 </span>Analysis of the Unconstrained or Centralized Iteration</h3>

<div id="A5.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We begin by analysing the behaviour of Algorithm <a href="#algofigure1" title="List of algofigures 1 ‣ 4 Emergent Algorithm ‣ Linear Transformers Implicitly DiscoverUnified Numerical Algorithms" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> in the ‘centralized’ setting of <math id="A5.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S=I_{n},M=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S=I_{n},M=1</annotation></semantics></math>. For simplicity, let us set <math id="A5.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta_{\ell}=\eta\|A_{\ell}\|_{2}^{-2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta_{\ell}=\eta\|A_{\ell}\|_{2}^{-2}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A5.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{\ell}=\gamma\|A_{\ell}\|_{2}^{-2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{\ell}=\gamma\|A_{\ell}\|_{2}^{-2}</annotation></semantics></math>—we will incorporate the specific structure of <math id="A5.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta,\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta,\gamma</annotation></semantics></math> later. Then we can write the iterations as</p>
<table id="A5.EGx3" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.E5"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle A_{\ell+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle A_{\ell+1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=A_{\ell}(I-\eta_{\ell}A_{\ell}^{\top}A_{\ell})," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=A_{\ell}(I-\eta_{\ell}A_{\ell}^{\top}A_{\ell}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(5)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex30"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle B_{\ell+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle B_{\ell+1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex30.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=B_{\ell}(I-\eta_{\ell}A_{\ell}^{\top}A_{\ell})," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=B_{\ell}(I-\eta_{\ell}A_{\ell}^{\top}A_{\ell}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex31"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle C_{\ell+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle C_{\ell+1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex31.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=(I-\gamma_{\ell}A_{\ell}A_{\ell}^{\top})C_{\ell}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=(I-\gamma_{\ell}A_{\ell}A_{\ell}^{\top})C_{\ell},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex32"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle D_{\ell+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle D_{\ell+1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex32.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=D_{\ell}+\gamma_{\ell}B_{\ell}A_{\ell}^{\top}C_{\ell}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=D_{\ell}+\gamma_{\ell}B_{\ell}A_{\ell}^{\top}C_{\ell}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Of course, we set <math id="A5.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{0},B_{0},C_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{0},B_{0},C_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> to be the observed blocks of the input matrix <math id="A5.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A5.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{0}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{0}=0</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="A5.SS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_bold ltx_font_italic">Useful Definitions.</em> We will analyze these iterations through the follow two objects</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmdefinition2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmdefinition2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 2</span></span><span id="Thmdefinition2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmdefinition2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmdefinition2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For <math id="Thmdefinition2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell\geq 0," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell\geq 0,</annotation></semantics></math> define the ‘signal energy’ <math id="Thmdefinition2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{\ell}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{\ell},</annotation></semantics></math> and the ‘signal correlation’ <math id="Thmdefinition2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}_{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}_{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math> as</p>
<table id="A5.Ex33" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{\ell}:=A_{\ell}A_{\ell}^{\top}\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times d}\textit{ and }\mathcal{V}_{\ell}:=B_{\ell}A_{\ell}^{\top}\in\mathbb{R}^{d^{\prime}\times d}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic"> and </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{\ell}:=A_{\ell}A_{\ell}^{\top}\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times d}\textit{ and }\mathcal{V}_{\ell}:=B_{\ell}A_{\ell}^{\top}\in\mathbb{R}^{d^{\prime}\times d}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">We further note the critical relationship that</p>
<table id="A5.Ex34" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex34.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{0}=W_{*}A_{0}\implies\mathcal{V}_{0}=W_{*}\mathcal{E}_{0})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">OPEN</mo><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟹</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{0}=W_{*}A_{0}\implies\mathcal{V}_{0}=W_{*}\mathcal{E}_{0}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.p4.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A5.SS1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{*}</annotation></semantics></math> is the Nyström parameter for the data matrix <math id="A5.SS1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> (see §<a href="#A1.SS1" title="A.1 Nyström Approximation ‣ Appendix A Methodological Details ‣ Linear Transformers Implicitly DiscoverUnified Numerical Algorithms" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.1</span></a>. An immediate consequence of the iterations above is the following dynamics.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 3</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Under the iterations of (<a href="#A5.E5" title="In E.1 Analysis of the Unconstrained or Centralized Iteration ‣ Appendix E Theoretical Analyses ‣ Linear Transformers Implicitly DiscoverUnified Numerical Algorithms" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>), we have the following dynamics</span></p>
<table id="A5.EGx4" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.E6"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{E}_{\ell+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{E}_{\ell+1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathcal{E}_{\ell}(I-\eta_{\ell}\mathcal{E}_{\ell})^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathcal{E}_{\ell}(I-\eta_{\ell}\mathcal{E}_{\ell})^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(6)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex35"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex35.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{V}_{\ell+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{V}_{\ell+1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex35.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathcal{V}_{\ell}(I-\eta_{\ell}\mathcal{E}_{\ell})^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathcal{V}_{\ell}(I-\eta_{\ell}\mathcal{E}_{\ell})^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex36"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex36.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle C_{\ell+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle C_{\ell+1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex36.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=(I-\gamma_{\ell}\mathcal{E}_{\ell})C_{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=(I-\gamma_{\ell}\mathcal{E}_{\ell})C_{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex37"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex37.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle D_{\ell+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle D_{\ell+1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex37.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=D_{\ell}+\gamma_{\ell}\mathcal{V}_{\ell}C_{\ell}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=D_{\ell}+\gamma_{\ell}\mathcal{V}_{\ell}C_{\ell},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem3.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem3.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="Thmtheorem3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>I</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I</annotation></semantics></math> is the <math id="Thmtheorem3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d\times d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d\times d</annotation></semantics></math> identity matrix.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem3.4" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem3.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">The <math id="Thmtheorem3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{\ell},C_{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\ell},C_{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math> iterations follow immediately by definition. For the former iterations, first observe that</span></p>
<table id="A5.EGx5" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.Ex38"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex38.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{V}_{\ell+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{V}_{\ell+1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex38.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=B_{\ell+1}A_{\ell+1}^{\top}=B_{\ell}(I-\eta_{\ell}A_{\ell}^{\top}A_{\ell})(I-\eta_{\ell}A_{\ell}^{\top}A_{\ell})A_{\ell}^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=B_{\ell+1}A_{\ell+1}^{\top}=B_{\ell}(I-\eta_{\ell}A_{\ell}^{\top}A_{\ell})(I-\eta_{\ell}A_{\ell}^{\top}A_{\ell})A_{\ell}^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex39"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex39.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=B_{\ell}(I-\eta_{\ell}A_{\ell}A_{\ell}^{\top})(A_{\ell}^{\top}-\eta_{\ell}A_{\ell}^{\top}A_{\ell}A_{\ell}^{\top})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=B_{\ell}(I-\eta_{\ell}A_{\ell}A_{\ell}^{\top})(A_{\ell}^{\top}-\eta_{\ell}A_{\ell}^{\top}A_{\ell}A_{\ell}^{\top})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex40"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex40.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=B_{\ell}(I-\eta_{\ell}A_{\ell}A_{\ell}^{\top})A_{\ell}^{\top}(I-\eta_{\ell}A_{\ell}A_{\ell}^{\top})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=B_{\ell}(I-\eta_{\ell}A_{\ell}A_{\ell}^{\top})A_{\ell}^{\top}(I-\eta_{\ell}A_{\ell}A_{\ell}^{\top})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex41"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex41.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=B_{\ell}A_{\ell}^{\top}(I-\eta_{\ell}A_{\ell}A_{\ell}^{\top})(I-\eta_{\ell}A_{\ell}A_{\ell}^{\top})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=B_{\ell}A_{\ell}^{\top}(I-\eta_{\ell}A_{\ell}A_{\ell}^{\top})(I-\eta_{\ell}A_{\ell}A_{\ell}^{\top})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex42"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex42.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathcal{V}_{\ell}(I-\eta_{\ell}\mathcal{E}_{\ell})^{2}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathcal{V}_{\ell}(I-\eta_{\ell}\mathcal{E}_{\ell})^{2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem3.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem3.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">where the first few inequalities arise by multiplying <math id="Thmtheorem3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{\ell}^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{\ell}^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math> from the right, and then factoring it out by the left, and the final is by definition. Similarly,</span></p>
<table id="A5.EGx6" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.Ex43"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex43.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{E}_{\ell+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{E}_{\ell+1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex43.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=A_{\ell+1}A_{\ell+1}^{\top}=A_{\ell}(I-\eta_{\ell}A_{\ell}^{\top}A_{\ell})(I-\eta_{\ell}A_{\ell}^{\top}A_{\ell})A_{\ell}^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=A_{\ell+1}A_{\ell+1}^{\top}=A_{\ell}(I-\eta_{\ell}A_{\ell}^{\top}A_{\ell})(I-\eta_{\ell}A_{\ell}^{\top}A_{\ell})A_{\ell}^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex44"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex44.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=A_{\ell}A_{\ell}^{\top}(I-\eta_{\ell}A_{\ell}A_{\ell}^{\top})^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=A_{\ell}A_{\ell}^{\top}(I-\eta_{\ell}A_{\ell}A_{\ell}^{\top})^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex45"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex45.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathcal{E}_{\ell}(I-\eta_{\ell}\mathcal{E}_{\ell})^{2}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathcal{E}_{\ell}(I-\eta_{\ell}\mathcal{E}_{\ell})^{2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem3.p2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem3.p2.3.1" class="ltx_text">where we reuse this transfer of <math id="Thmtheorem3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{\ell}^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{\ell}^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math> from the right to the left, and then use the definition of <math id="Thmtheorem3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS1.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS1.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Note from the above expression that for any <math id="A5.SS1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell^{\prime}&gt;\ell,\mathcal{E}_{\ell^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>&gt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell^{\prime}&gt;\ell,\mathcal{E}_{\ell^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math> is a polynomial in <math id="A5.SS1.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math>. As a result, <math id="A5.SS1.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.SS1.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{\ell^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{\ell^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math> commute for all pairs <math id="A5.SS1.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\ell,\ell^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\ell,\ell^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS1.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS1.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="A5.SS1.p6.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_bold ltx_font_italic">Telescoping the Error.</em> For the sake of conciseness in the further expressions, we further introduce the following notation.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmdefinition3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmdefinition3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 3</span></span><span id="Thmdefinition3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmdefinition3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmdefinition3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Define <math id="Thmdefinition3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{\ell}:=\prod_{l&lt;\ell}(I-\eta_{l}\mathcal{E}_{l})^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">:=</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0em">∏</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{\ell}:=\prod_{l&lt;\ell}(I-\eta_{l}\mathcal{E}_{l})^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmdefinition3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{\ell}^{\top}:=\prod_{l&lt;\ell}(I-\gamma_{l}\mathcal{E}_{l})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>N</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo rspace="0.111em">:=</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0em">∏</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{\ell}^{\top}:=\prod_{l&lt;\ell}(I-\gamma_{l}\mathcal{E}_{l})</annotation></semantics></math>, where we use the convention that</p>
<table id="A5.Ex46" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex46.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\prod_{l&lt;\ell}U_{l}=U_{1}U_{2}\cdots U_{\ell-1}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></msub><mi>U</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>U</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mi>U</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>U</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\prod_{l&lt;\ell}U_{l}=U_{1}U_{2}\cdots U_{\ell-1},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmdefinition3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">and <math id="Thmdefinition3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{0}=N_{0}=I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{0}=N_{0}=I</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS1.p7" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS1.p7.1" class="ltx_p">By Lemma <a href="#Thmtheorem3" title="Lemma 3. ‣ E.1 Analysis of the Unconstrained or Centralized Iteration ‣ Appendix E Theoretical Analyses ‣ Linear Transformers Implicitly DiscoverUnified Numerical Algorithms" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>, we have <math id="A5.SS1.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{\ell}=\mathcal{E}_{0}M_{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{\ell}=\mathcal{E}_{0}M_{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.SS1.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}_{\ell}=\mathcal{V}_{0}M_{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}_{\ell}=\mathcal{V}_{0}M_{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math>. Further, <math id="A5.SS1.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{\ell}=N_{\ell}C_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{\ell}=N_{\ell}C_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>.<span id="footnote1" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">1</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">1</sup>
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">1</span>
              
              
              
            Note that the order of multiplication is flipped here, which follows notationally since we defined the transpose <math id="footnote1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{\ell}^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>N</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{\ell}^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math> above. Of course, all the <math id="footnote1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{l}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{l}</annotation></semantics></math> commute, so this is not very important in this case, but this subtle distinction will matter more in subsequent analysis.</span></span></span></p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS1.p8" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS1.p8.1" class="ltx_p">This leads to the following estimate of the value of <math id="A5.SS1.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>D</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 4</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmtheorem4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmtheorem4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{*}</annotation></semantics></math> be the Nyström regression parameter for the data <math id="Thmtheorem4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(A,B)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(A,B)</annotation></semantics></math>. For any <math id="Thmtheorem4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell\geq 0," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell\geq 0,</annotation></semantics></math> we have</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex47" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex47.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{\ell}=W_{*}(I-N_{\ell})C_{0}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\ell}=W_{*}(I-N_{\ell})C_{0}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem4.4" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem4.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmtheorem4.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem4.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="Thmtheorem4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{0}=0," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{0}=0,</annotation></semantics></math> we have</span></p>
<table id="A5.EGx7" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.Ex48"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex48.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle D_{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>D</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle D_{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex48.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{l&lt;\ell}\gamma_{l}\mathcal{V}_{l}C_{l}=\mathcal{V}_{0}\left(\sum_{l&lt;\ell}\gamma_{l}M_{l}N_{l}\right)C_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{l&lt;\ell}\gamma_{l}\mathcal{V}_{l}C_{l}=\mathcal{V}_{0}\left(\sum_{l&lt;\ell}\gamma_{l}M_{l}N_{l}\right)C_{0}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex50"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex50.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=W_{*}\mathcal{E}_{0}\left(\sum_{l&lt;\ell}\gamma_{l}M_{l}N_{l}\right)C_{0}=W_{*}\left(\sum_{l&lt;\ell}\gamma_{l}\mathcal{E}_{0}M_{l}N_{l}\right)C_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=W_{*}\mathcal{E}_{0}\left(\sum_{l&lt;\ell}\gamma_{l}M_{l}N_{l}\right)C_{0}=W_{*}\left(\sum_{l&lt;\ell}\gamma_{l}\mathcal{E}_{0}M_{l}N_{l}\right)C_{0}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex51"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex51.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=W_{*}\left(\sum_{l&lt;\ell}\gamma_{l}\mathcal{E}_{l}N_{l}\right)C_{0}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=W_{*}\left(\sum_{l&lt;\ell}\gamma_{l}\mathcal{E}_{l}N_{l}\right)C_{0},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem4.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem4.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">where we used the definition of <math id="Thmtheorem4.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>M</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math>. But now, using the definition of <math id="Thmtheorem4.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>N</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math>, notice that for any <math id="Thmtheorem4.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>l</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex52" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex52.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{l+1}^{\top}=N_{l}^{\top}(I-\gamma_{l}\mathcal{E}_{l})\iff N_{l+1}=N_{l}-\gamma_{l}\mathcal{E}_{l}N_{l}\iff\gamma_{l}\mathcal{E}_{l}N_{l}=N_{l}-N_{l+1}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>N</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>N</mi><mi>l</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⇔</mo><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⇔</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{l+1}^{\top}=N_{l}^{\top}(I-\gamma_{l}\mathcal{E}_{l})\iff N_{l+1}=N_{l}-\gamma_{l}\mathcal{E}_{l}N_{l}\iff\gamma_{l}\mathcal{E}_{l}N_{l}=N_{l}-N_{l+1}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem4.p2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem4.p2.3.1" class="ltx_text">Consequently, we can write</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex53" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex53.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{\ell}=W_{*}\left(\sum_{l&lt;\ell}(N_{l}-N_{l+1})\right)C_{0}=W_{*}(I-N_{\ell})C_{0}.\qed" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">.</mo><mo class="ltx_mathvariant_italic" lspace="0.0835em" mathvariant="italic" separator="true">∎</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\ell}=W_{*}\left(\sum_{l&lt;\ell}(N_{l}-N_{l+1})\right)C_{0}=W_{*}(I-N_{\ell})C_{0}.\qed</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS1.p9" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS1.p9.1" class="ltx_p">Recall that <math id="A5.SS1.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{D}_{*}=W_{*}C_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>D</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{D}_{*}=W_{*}C_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>, meaning that the error <math id="A5.SS1.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{\ell}-\hat{D}_{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>D</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>∗</mo></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\ell}-\hat{D}_{*}</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A5.SS1.p9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{*}N_{\ell}C_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{*}N_{\ell}C_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus, this lemma captures a basic fact: as the size of the matrix <math id="A5.SS1.p9.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>N</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math> decays, the output <math id="A5.SS1.p9.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>D</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math> gets closer to the target output <math id="A5.SS1.p9.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{D}_{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>D</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>∗</mo></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{D}_{*}</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus, our main focus is to characterize the decay of this matrix. We shall show this by arguing that the matrices <math id="A5.SS1.p9.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math> quickly become well-conditioned through the course of the iterations, and consequently <math id="A5.SS1.p9.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>N</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math> decays quickly.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS1.p10" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS1.p10.1" class="ltx_p">Before proceeding, note that in general, <math id="A5.SS1.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> may have zero eigenvalues, which are left unchanged by the main dynamics (see below), meaning that <math id="A5.SS1.p10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I-N_{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I-N_{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math> may even asymptotically have a large eigenvalue corresponding to vectors in the kernel of <math id="A5.SS1.p10.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>. However, we observe that <math id="A5.SS1.p10.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{*}=\mathcal{V}_{0}\mathcal{E}_{0}^{\dagger}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mn>0</mn><mo>†</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{*}=\mathcal{V}_{0}\mathcal{E}_{0}^{\dagger},</annotation></semantics></math> and thus any energy in <math id="A5.SS1.p10.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> that lies in the kernel of <math id="A5.SS1.p10.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> is irrelevant to the prediction <math id="A5.SS1.p10.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{D}_{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>D</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>∗</mo></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{D}_{*}</annotation></semantics></math>. As such, it is equivalent for us to analyse the two-norm of the matrix <math id="A5.SS1.p10.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{N}_{\ell}:=(I-P_{0})N_{\ell}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>N</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{N}_{\ell}:=(I-P_{0})N_{\ell},</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="A5.SS1.p10.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> projects onto the kernel of <math id="A5.SS1.p10.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>. Instead of this notational complication, we will henceforth just assume that <math id="A5.SS1.p10.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> is full rank (i.e., all of its eigenvalues are nonzero), and mention where changes need to be made to handle the general case.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS1.p11" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS1.p11.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="A5.SS1.p11.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_bold ltx_font_italic">Conditioning of <math id="A5.SS1.p11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math></em><span id="A5.SS1.p11.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span> Let us then begin with some notation: for a positive (semi-)definite symmetric matrix <math id="A5.SS1.p11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M},</annotation></semantics></math> we let <math id="A5.SS1.p11.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda^{i}(\mathcal{M})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda^{i}(\mathcal{M})</annotation></semantics></math> denote its <math id="A5.SS1.p11.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>th largest eigenvalue, <math id="A5.SS1.p11.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{\lambda}(\mathcal{M})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{\lambda}(\mathcal{M})</annotation></semantics></math> denote its largest eigenvalue, and <math id="A5.SS1.p11.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{\lambda}(\mathcal{M})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder accentunder="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{\lambda}(\mathcal{M})</annotation></semantics></math> denote its smallest (nonzero) eigenvalue. Notice that <math id="A5.SS1.p11.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{\lambda}(\cdot)=\lambda^{1}(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>λ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{\lambda}(\cdot)=\lambda^{1}(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A5.SS1.p11.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{\lambda}(\mathcal{M})=\lambda^{r}(\mathcal{M})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><munder accentunder="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>λ</mi><mi>r</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{\lambda}(\mathcal{M})=\lambda^{r}(\mathcal{M})</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A5.SS1.p11.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math> is the rank of <math id="A5.SS1.p11.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}</annotation></semantics></math> (we will work with full rank <math id="A5.SS1.p11.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}</annotation></semantics></math>, but be cognizant of rank sensitivity). Let <math id="A5.SS1.p11.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v^{i}(\mathcal{M})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v^{i}(\mathcal{M})</annotation></semantics></math> denote the corresponding eigenvector. We further introduce the notation</p>
<table id="A5.Ex54" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex54.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\lambda^{i}_{\ell}=\lambda^{i}(\mathcal{E}_{\ell}),\quad\overline{\lambda}_{\ell}=\overline{\lambda}(\mathcal{E}_{\ell}),\quad\textit{and }\quad\underline{\lambda}_{\ell}=\underline{\lambda}(\mathcal{E}_{\ell})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">and </mtext><msub><munder accentunder="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><munder accentunder="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda^{i}_{\ell}=\lambda^{i}(\mathcal{E}_{\ell}),\quad\overline{\lambda}_{\ell}=\overline{\lambda}(\mathcal{E}_{\ell}),\quad\textit{and }\quad\underline{\lambda}_{\ell}=\underline{\lambda}(\mathcal{E}_{\ell}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS1.p12" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS1.p12.1" class="ltx_p">Our first observation is that the iterations leave the eigenstructure of <math id="A5.SS1.p12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math> undisturbed.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem5" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 5</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Suppose that <math id="Thmtheorem5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> is an eigenvector of <math id="Thmtheorem5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then it is also an eigenvector of <math id="Thmtheorem5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math> for any <math id="Thmtheorem5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>. Further, if <math id="Thmtheorem5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v\in\mathrm{ker}(\mathcal{E}_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>ker</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\in\mathrm{ker}(\mathcal{E}_{0})</annotation></semantics></math> then <math id="Thmtheorem5.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v\in\mathrm{ker}(\mathcal{E}_{\ell})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>ker</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\in\mathrm{ker}(\mathcal{E}_{\ell})</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem5.4" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem5.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem5.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem5.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">We have <math id="Thmtheorem5.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{0}^{n}v=\lambda^{n}v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>λ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{0}^{n}v=\lambda^{n}v</annotation></semantics></math>. But note that <math id="Thmtheorem5.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math> is some polynomial in <math id="Thmtheorem5.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{0}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{0},</annotation></semantics></math> i.e., for some finite number of coefficients <math id="Thmtheorem5.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="Thmtheorem5.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{\ell}v=\sum_{n\geq 0}\alpha_{n}\mathcal{E}_{0}^{n}v=(\sum_{n\geq 0}\alpha_{n}\lambda^{n})v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>λ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{\ell}v=\sum_{n\geq 0}\alpha_{n}\mathcal{E}_{0}^{n}v=(\sum_{n\geq 0}\alpha_{n}\lambda^{n})v</annotation></semantics></math>, and the claim follows. Crucially, observe that since <math id="Thmtheorem5.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{\ell}=M_{\ell}\mathcal{E}_{0}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{\ell}=M_{\ell}\mathcal{E}_{0},</annotation></semantics></math> we have <math id="Thmtheorem5.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{0}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{0}=0</annotation></semantics></math>, and so if <math id="Thmtheorem5.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{0}v=0," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{0}v=0,</annotation></semantics></math> then <math id="Thmtheorem5.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{\ell}v=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{\ell}v=0</annotation></semantics></math> as well.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS1.p13" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS1.p13.1" class="ltx_p">Since the eigenstructure of <math id="A5.SS1.p13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> is preserved, we can begin to study the behaviour of its eigenvalues in a simplified way. The critical relationship for our analysis is the following iterative structure on the largest and smallest (nonzero) eigenvalues of <math id="A5.SS1.p13.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem6" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 6</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem6.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem6.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmtheorem6.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Suppose that <math id="Thmtheorem6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\forall\ell,\eta_{\ell}\leq\overline{\lambda}_{\ell}^{-1}/3." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\forall\ell,\eta_{\ell}\leq\overline{\lambda}_{\ell}^{-1}/3.</annotation></semantics></math> Then for all <math id="Thmtheorem6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell,</annotation></semantics></math></span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex55" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex55.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{\lambda}_{\ell+1}=(1-\eta_{\ell}\overline{\lambda}_{\ell})^{2}\overline{\lambda}_{\ell}\quad\textit{ and }\quad\underline{\lambda}_{\ell+1}=(1-\eta_{\ell}\underline{\lambda}_{\ell})^{2}\underline{\lambda}_{\ell}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic"> and </mtext><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><msub><munder accentunder="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><munder accentunder="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><munder accentunder="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{\lambda}_{\ell+1}=(1-\eta_{\ell}\overline{\lambda}_{\ell})^{2}\overline{\lambda}_{\ell}\quad\textit{ and }\quad\underline{\lambda}_{\ell+1}=(1-\eta_{\ell}\underline{\lambda}_{\ell})^{2}\underline{\lambda}_{\ell}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem6.4" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem6.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmtheorem6.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem6.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Suppose <math id="Thmtheorem6.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u^{1},u^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>u</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u^{1},u^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> are two eigenvectors of <math id="Thmtheorem6.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>, with positive eigenvalues <math id="Thmtheorem6.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{0},\nu_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ν</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{0},\nu_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>. Since <math id="Thmtheorem6.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u^{1},u^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>u</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u^{1},u^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> are also eigenvectors of <math id="Thmtheorem6.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{\ell}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{\ell},</annotation></semantics></math> denote the eigenvalues for the latter as <math id="Thmtheorem6.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{\ell},\nu_{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ν</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{\ell},\nu_{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math>. Note that these remain nonnegative. Indeed, by multiplying the dynamics for <math id="Thmtheorem6.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{\ell+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{\ell+1}</annotation></semantics></math> by, say, <math id="Thmtheorem6.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u^{1}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u^{1},</annotation></semantics></math> we have</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex56" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex56.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{\ell+1}u^{1}=\mathcal{E}_{\ell+1}u^{1}=\mathcal{E}_{\ell}(I-\eta_{\ell}\mathcal{E}_{\ell})^{2}u^{1}=(1-\eta_{\ell}\mu_{\ell})^{2}\mu_{\ell}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>u</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>u</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>u</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{\ell+1}u^{1}=\mathcal{E}_{\ell+1}u^{1}=\mathcal{E}_{\ell}(I-\eta_{\ell}\mathcal{E}_{\ell})^{2}u^{1}=(1-\eta_{\ell}\mu_{\ell})^{2}\mu_{\ell},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem6.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem6.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">and similarly for <math id="Thmtheorem6.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu_{\ell}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ν</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu_{\ell}.</annotation></semantics></math> We will first inductively show that if <math id="Thmtheorem6.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{0}&gt;\nu_{0}\iff\mu_{\ell}&gt;\nu_{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><msub><mi>ν</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">⇔</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><msub><mi>ν</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{0}&gt;\nu_{0}\iff\mu_{\ell}&gt;\nu_{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="Thmtheorem6.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell</annotation></semantics></math>. In other words, not only are the eigenvectors of <math id="Thmtheorem6.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> stable under the iterations, but also the ordering of the eigenvalues.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem6.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmtheorem6.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem6.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">We thus note that the claim follows directly from this result. Indeed, let <math id="Thmtheorem6.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>v</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v^{1}</annotation></semantics></math> be the eigenvector corresponding to <math id="Thmtheorem6.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{\lambda}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{\lambda}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then we see that it remains eigenvector corresponding to <math id="Thmtheorem6.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{\lambda}_{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{\lambda}_{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="Thmtheorem6.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell</annotation></semantics></math>. But then using our observation above with <math id="Thmtheorem6.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u^{1}=v^{1}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>v</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u^{1}=v^{1},</annotation></semantics></math> we get the result for <math id="Thmtheorem6.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{\lambda}_{\ell+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{\lambda}_{\ell+1}</annotation></semantics></math>. A similar argument works for <math id="Thmtheorem6.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{\lambda}_{\ell+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><munder accentunder="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{\lambda}_{\ell+1}</annotation></semantics></math>. Note that nothing per se demands that these eigenvalues have unit multiplicity, and the argument is completely insensitive to this.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem6.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmtheorem6.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem6.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">To see the ordering claim on <math id="Thmtheorem6.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{\ell},\nu_{\ell}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ν</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{\ell},\nu_{\ell},</annotation></semantics></math> then, we observe that</span></p>
<table id="A5.EGx8" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.Ex57"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex57.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mu_{\ell+1}-\nu_{\ell+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ν</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mu_{\ell+1}-\nu_{\ell+1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex57.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=(1-\eta_{\ell}\mu_{\ell})^{2}\mu_{\ell}-(1-\eta_{\ell}\nu_{\ell})^{2}\nu_{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ν</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ν</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=(1-\eta_{\ell}\mu_{\ell})^{2}\mu_{\ell}-(1-\eta_{\ell}\nu_{\ell})^{2}\nu_{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex58"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex58.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=(\mu_{\ell}-\nu_{\ell})-2\eta(\mu_{\ell}^{2}-\nu_{\ell}^{2})+\eta^{2}(\mu_{\ell}^{3}-\nu_{\ell}^{3})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ν</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>ν</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>3</mn></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>ν</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>3</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=(\mu_{\ell}-\nu_{\ell})-2\eta(\mu_{\ell}^{2}-\nu_{\ell}^{2})+\eta^{2}(\mu_{\ell}^{3}-\nu_{\ell}^{3})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex59"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex59.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=(\mu_{\ell}-\nu_{\ell})\left(1-2\eta_{\ell}(\mu_{\ell}+\nu_{\ell})+\eta_{\ell}^{2}(\mu_{\ell}^{2}+\nu_{\ell}^{2}+\mu_{\ell}\nu_{\ell})\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ν</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>ν</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>η</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>ν</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ν</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=(\mu_{\ell}-\nu_{\ell})\left(1-2\eta_{\ell}(\mu_{\ell}+\nu_{\ell})+\eta_{\ell}^{2}(\mu_{\ell}^{2}+\nu_{\ell}^{2}+\mu_{\ell}\nu_{\ell})\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem6.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem6.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">Now, if the term multiplying <math id="Thmtheorem6.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mu_{\ell}-\nu_{\ell})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ν</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mu_{\ell}-\nu_{\ell})</annotation></semantics></math> is nonnegative, then the claim follows. To see when this occurs, let us set <math id="Thmtheorem6.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta_{\ell}=\eta\overline{\lambda}_{\ell}^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta_{\ell}=\eta\overline{\lambda}_{\ell}^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math>, and pull <math id="Thmtheorem6.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{\lambda}^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{\lambda}^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math> within the brackets. We are left with an expression of the form</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex60" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex60.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(1-2\eta(x+y)+\eta^{2}(x^{2}+y^{2}+xy))," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1-2\eta(x+y)+\eta^{2}(x^{2}+y^{2}+xy)),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem6.p4.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem6.p4.3.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="Thmtheorem6.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x,y)\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x,y)\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math>. For <math id="Thmtheorem6.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta\leq 2/3," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta\leq 2/3,</annotation></semantics></math> the minimum over this range occurs when <math id="Thmtheorem6.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x=y=1," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x=y=1,</annotation></semantics></math> and takes the value</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex61" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex61.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-4\eta+3\eta^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-4\eta+3\eta^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem6.p4.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem6.p4.4.1" class="ltx_text">It is a triviality to show that this function is nonnegative for <math id="Thmtheorem6.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta\leq 1/3," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta\leq 1/3,</annotation></semantics></math> and so we are done.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS1.p14" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS1.p14.1" class="ltx_p">With this in hand, we will argue that <math id="A5.SS1.p14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{\lambda}_{\ell}\to\overline{\lambda}_{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><munder accentunder="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{\lambda}_{\ell}\to\overline{\lambda}_{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math> at a quadratic convergence rate after an initial burn-in period. Of course, this is equivalent to saying that <math id="A5.SS1.p14.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa_{\ell}:=\overline{\lambda}_{\ell}/\underline{\lambda}_{\ell}\to 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>κ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><msub><munder accentunder="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa_{\ell}:=\overline{\lambda}_{\ell}/\underline{\lambda}_{\ell}\to 1</annotation></semantics></math>. Notice that this <math id="A5.SS1.p14.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa_{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>κ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa_{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math> is precisely the condition number of <math id="A5.SS1.p14.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math> (which in turn is the square of the condition number of <math id="A5.SS1.p14.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math> mentioned in our discussion in §<a href="#S5" title="5 Evaluation of EAGLE ‣ Linear Transformers Implicitly DiscoverUnified Numerical Algorithms" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>).</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem7" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem7.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 7</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem7.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem7.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem7.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Define <math id="Thmtheorem7.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa_{\ell}=\overline{\lambda}_{\ell}/\underline{\lambda}_{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>κ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><msub><munder accentunder="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa_{\ell}=\overline{\lambda}_{\ell}/\underline{\lambda}_{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="Thmtheorem7.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{\ell}=\kappa_{\ell}-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>κ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{\ell}=\kappa_{\ell}-1</annotation></semantics></math>. If <math id="Thmtheorem7.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta_{\ell}\leq\overline{\lambda}^{-1}/3," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta_{\ell}\leq\overline{\lambda}^{-1}/3,</annotation></semantics></math> then <math id="Thmtheorem7.p1.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\theta_{\ell+1}\leq\theta_{\ell}\exp(-5\eta_{\ell}\overline{\lambda}_{\ell}/3)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mn>5</mn><msub><mi>η</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{\ell+1}\leq\theta_{\ell}\exp(-5\eta_{\ell}\overline{\lambda}_{\ell}/3)</annotation></semantics></math>. Further, if <math id="Thmtheorem7.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta_{\ell}\overline{\lambda}_{\ell}=1/3," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta_{\ell}\overline{\lambda}_{\ell}=1/3,</annotation></semantics></math> then <math id="Thmtheorem7.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{\ell+1}\leq 3\theta_{\ell}^{2}/4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{\ell+1}\leq 3\theta_{\ell}^{2}/4</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem7.4" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem7.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmtheorem7.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem7.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">For the sake of succinctness, let us write <math id="Thmtheorem7.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta_{\ell}=\eta,\overline{\lambda}_{\ell}=\overline{\lambda},\underline{\lambda}_{\ell}=\underline{\lambda},\theta_{\ell}=\theta," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><munder accentunder="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><munder accentunder="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta_{\ell}=\eta,\overline{\lambda}_{\ell}=\overline{\lambda},\underline{\lambda}_{\ell}=\underline{\lambda},\theta_{\ell}=\theta,</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmtheorem7.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{\ell+1}=\theta_{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mo>+</mo></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{\ell+1}=\theta_{+}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then, using the previous lemma, we can write</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex62" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex62.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa_{\ell+1}=\theta_{+}+1=(\theta+1)\left(\frac{1-\eta\overline{\lambda}}{1-\eta\underline{\lambda}}\right)^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>κ</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><munder accentunder="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa_{\ell+1}=\theta_{+}+1=(\theta+1)\left(\frac{1-\eta\overline{\lambda}}{1-\eta\underline{\lambda}}\right)^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem7.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem7.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">But notice that</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex63" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex63.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1-\eta\overline{\lambda}}{1-\eta\underline{\lambda}}=1+\eta\frac{\overline{\lambda}-\underline{\lambda}}{1-\eta\underline{\lambda}}=1-\eta\frac{\overline{\lambda}(1-1/(\theta+1))}{1-\eta\overline{\lambda}/(\theta+1)}=1-\frac{\theta\eta\overline{\lambda}}{\theta+1-\eta\overline{\lambda}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><munder accentunder="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><munder accentunder="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><munder accentunder="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1-\eta\overline{\lambda}}{1-\eta\underline{\lambda}}=1+\eta\frac{\overline{\lambda}-\underline{\lambda}}{1-\eta\underline{\lambda}}=1-\eta\frac{\overline{\lambda}(1-1/(\theta+1))}{1-\eta\overline{\lambda}/(\theta+1)}=1-\frac{\theta\eta\overline{\lambda}}{\theta+1-\eta\overline{\lambda}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem7.p2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem7.p2.3.1" class="ltx_text">Thus,</span></p>
<table id="A5.EGx9" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.Ex64"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex64.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\theta_{+}+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\theta_{+}+1</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex64.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=(\theta+1)\left(1-2\frac{\theta\eta\overline{\lambda}}{(\theta+1-\eta\overline{\lambda})}+\frac{\theta^{2}\eta^{2}\overline{\lambda}^{2}}{(\theta+1-\eta\overline{\lambda})^{2}}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>θ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=(\theta+1)\left(1-2\frac{\theta\eta\overline{\lambda}}{(\theta+1-\eta\overline{\lambda})}+\frac{\theta^{2}\eta^{2}\overline{\lambda}^{2}}{(\theta+1-\eta\overline{\lambda})^{2}}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex65"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex65.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\theta+1-\theta\frac{\eta\overline{\lambda}}{1-\eta\underline{\lambda}}\left(2-\frac{\theta\eta\overline{\lambda}}{(\theta+1-\eta\overline{\lambda})}\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><munder accentunder="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\theta+1-\theta\frac{\eta\overline{\lambda}}{1-\eta\underline{\lambda}}\left(2-\frac{\theta\eta\overline{\lambda}}{(\theta+1-\eta\overline{\lambda})}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem7.p2.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem7.p2.4.1" class="ltx_text">But the bracketed term is nonincreasing in <math id="Thmtheorem7.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta\overline{\lambda}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta\overline{\lambda}</annotation></semantics></math> (in the negative term, the numerator increases and the denominator decreases with this value), and so</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex66" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex66.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2-\frac{\theta\eta\overline{\lambda}}{\theta+1-\eta\overline{\lambda}}\geq 2-\frac{\theta}{3\theta+3-1}=\frac{5\theta+4}{3\theta+2}\geq\frac{5}{3}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>≥</mo><mfrac><mn>5</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2-\frac{\theta\eta\overline{\lambda}}{\theta+1-\eta\overline{\lambda}}\geq 2-\frac{\theta}{3\theta+3-1}=\frac{5\theta+4}{3\theta+2}\geq\frac{5}{3}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem7.p2.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem7.p2.5.1" class="ltx_text">Thus, we have</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex67" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex67.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{\ell+1}\leq\theta_{\ell}-\theta_{\ell}\cdot\frac{5/3\eta_{\ell}\overline{\lambda}_{\ell}}{1-\eta_{\ell}\underline{\lambda}_{\ell}}\implies\theta_{\ell+1}\leq\theta_{\ell}\exp\left(-\frac{5\eta_{\ell}\overline{\lambda}_{\ell}/3}{1-\eta_{\ell}\underline{\lambda}_{\ell}}\right)\leq\theta_{\ell}\exp(-\eta_{\ell}\overline{\lambda}_{\ell})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><munder accentunder="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟹</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><munder accentunder="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{\ell+1}\leq\theta_{\ell}-\theta_{\ell}\cdot\frac{5/3\eta_{\ell}\overline{\lambda}_{\ell}}{1-\eta_{\ell}\underline{\lambda}_{\ell}}\implies\theta_{\ell+1}\leq\theta_{\ell}\exp\left(-\frac{5\eta_{\ell}\overline{\lambda}_{\ell}/3}{1-\eta_{\ell}\underline{\lambda}_{\ell}}\right)\leq\theta_{\ell}\exp(-\eta_{\ell}\overline{\lambda}_{\ell}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem7.p2.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem7.p2.6.1" class="ltx_text">On the other hand (going back to the notation that suppresses <math id="Thmtheorem7.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell</annotation></semantics></math>), if we set <math id="Thmtheorem7.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta\overline{\lambda}=L," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta\overline{\lambda}=L,</annotation></semantics></math> then since</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex68" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex68.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1-\eta\overline{\lambda}}{1-\eta\underline{\lambda}}=\frac{1-L}{(\theta+1-L)/(\theta+1)}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><munder accentunder="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1-\eta\overline{\lambda}}{1-\eta\underline{\lambda}}=\frac{1-L}{(\theta+1-L)/(\theta+1)},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem7.p2.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem7.p2.7.1" class="ltx_text">we find by doing the long multiplication that</span></p>
<table id="A5.EGx10" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.Ex69"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex69.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle(\theta_{+}+1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle(\theta_{+}+1)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex69.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{(\theta+1)^{3}(1-L)^{2}}{(\theta+1-L)^{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>3</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{(\theta+1)^{3}(1-L)^{2}}{(\theta+1-L)^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex70"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex70.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\iff\theta_{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo stretchy="false">⇔</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mo>+</mo></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\iff\theta_{+}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex70.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\theta(1-4L+3L^{2})+\theta^{2}(2-6L+3L^{2})+\theta^{3}(1-L)^{2}}{(\theta+1-L)^{2}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>θ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>θ</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\theta(1-4L+3L^{2})+\theta^{2}(2-6L+3L^{2})+\theta^{3}(1-L)^{2}}{(\theta+1-L)^{2}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem7.p2.8" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem7.p2.8.1" class="ltx_text">Setting <math id="Thmtheorem7.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L=\eta_{\ell}\overline{\lambda}_{\ell}=1/3," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L=\eta_{\ell}\overline{\lambda}_{\ell}=1/3,</annotation></semantics></math> the linear term in <math id="Thmtheorem7.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math> vanishes, and we end up with</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex71" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex71.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{+}=\frac{\theta^{2}/3+4\theta^{3}/9}{(\theta+2/3)^{2}}=\theta^{2}\cdot\frac{4\theta+3}{(3\theta+2)^{2}}\leq\frac{3\theta^{2}}{4}.\qed" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>θ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>9</mn></mrow></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>θ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">.</mo><mo class="ltx_mathvariant_italic" lspace="0.0835em" mathvariant="italic" separator="true">∎</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{+}=\frac{\theta^{2}/3+4\theta^{3}/9}{(\theta+2/3)^{2}}=\theta^{2}\cdot\frac{4\theta+3}{(3\theta+2)^{2}}\leq\frac{3\theta^{2}}{4}.\qed</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS1.p15" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS1.p15.1" class="ltx_p">The statement of this Lemma has shown two decay modes of <math id="A5.SS1.p15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{\ell}=(\kappa_{\ell}-1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>κ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{\ell}=(\kappa_{\ell}-1)</annotation></semantics></math>. Firstly, as long as <math id="A5.SS1.p15.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta_{\ell}\leq\overline{\lambda}^{-1}_{\ell}/3," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta_{\ell}\leq\overline{\lambda}^{-1}_{\ell}/3,</annotation></semantics></math> this quantity decays at least at a linear rate. Further, if <math id="A5.SS1.p15.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta_{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>η</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta_{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math> is set to exactly <math id="A5.SS1.p15.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{\lambda}^{-1}_{\ell}/3," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{\lambda}^{-1}_{\ell}/3,</annotation></semantics></math> then once <math id="A5.SS1.p15.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math> dips below <math id="A5.SS1.p15.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>, which occurs after about <math id="A5.SS1.p15.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3\log(\theta_{0})/5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3\log(\theta_{0})/5</annotation></semantics></math> iterations, we can exploit the quadratic bound in <math id="A5.SS1.p15.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math> to recover a stronger convergence rate. Together, this yields the following convergence behaviour for <math id="A5.SS1.p15.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa_{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>κ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa_{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem8" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem8.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 8</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem8.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem8.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmtheorem8.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem8.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmtheorem8.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa_{\ell}:=\overline{\lambda}_{\ell}/\underline{\lambda}_{\ell}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>κ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><msub><munder accentunder="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa_{\ell}:=\overline{\lambda}_{\ell}/\underline{\lambda}_{\ell}.</annotation></semantics></math> If for all <math id="Thmtheorem8.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell,</annotation></semantics></math> <math id="Thmtheorem8.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta_{\ell}\overline{\lambda}=1/3," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta_{\ell}\overline{\lambda}=1/3,</annotation></semantics></math> then <math id="Thmtheorem8.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa_{\ell}-1\leq\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>κ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa_{\ell}-1\leq\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math> for all</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex72" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex72.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell\geq L=2+\lceil(3/5)\log(\kappa_{0})\rceil+\lceil\log_{2}(\log(4/3\varepsilon))\rceil." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>≥</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌈</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>κ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌉</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>log</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌉</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell\geq L=2+\lceil(3/5)\log(\kappa_{0})\rceil+\lceil\log_{2}(\log(4/3\varepsilon))\rceil.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem8.4" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem8.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmtheorem8.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem8.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">First using the geometric decay in Lemma <a href="#Thmtheorem7" title="Lemma 7. ‣ E.1 Analysis of the Unconstrained or Centralized Iteration ‣ Appendix E Theoretical Analyses ‣ Linear Transformers Implicitly DiscoverUnified Numerical Algorithms" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>, we know that <math id="Thmtheorem8.p2.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\theta_{\ell}\leq(\kappa_{0}-1)\exp(-5(\ell-1)/3)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>κ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mn>5</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{\ell}\leq(\kappa_{0}-1)\exp(-5(\ell-1)/3).</annotation></semantics></math> Set <math id="Thmtheorem8.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{0}=2+3/5\log(\kappa_{0}-1)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>κ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{0}=2+3/5\log(\kappa_{0}-1).</annotation></semantics></math> Then for <math id="Thmtheorem8.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell\geq\ell_{0}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell\geq\ell_{0},</annotation></semantics></math> we have <math id="Thmtheorem8.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{\ell_{0}}\leq 1/e" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{\ell_{0}}\leq 1/e</annotation></semantics></math>. Further, for iterations beyond this <math id="Thmtheorem8.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{0}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{0},</annotation></semantics></math> the supergeometric decay <math id="Thmtheorem8.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{\ell+1}\leq 3\theta_{\ell}^{2}/4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{\ell+1}\leq 3\theta_{\ell}^{2}/4</annotation></semantics></math> in Lemma <a href="#Thmtheorem7" title="Lemma 7. ‣ E.1 Analysis of the Unconstrained or Centralized Iteration ‣ Appendix E Theoretical Analyses ‣ Linear Transformers Implicitly DiscoverUnified Numerical Algorithms" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a> implies that</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex73" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex73.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3\theta_{\ell+1}/4\leq(3\theta_{\ell}/4)^{2}\iff T_{\ell+1}\leq 2T_{\ell}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">⇔</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3\theta_{\ell+1}/4\leq(3\theta_{\ell}/4)^{2}\iff T_{\ell+1}\leq 2T_{\ell},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem8.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem8.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="Thmtheorem8.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{\ell}:=\log(3\theta_{\ell}/4)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{\ell}:=\log(3\theta_{\ell}/4)</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus,</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex74" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex74.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{\ell}\leq 2^{\ell-\ell_{0}}T_{\ell_{0}}\leq-2^{\ell-\ell_{0}}\implies\theta_{\ell}\leq 4/3\exp(-2^{\ell-\ell_{0}})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟹</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{\ell}\leq 2^{\ell-\ell_{0}}T_{\ell_{0}}\leq-2^{\ell-\ell_{0}}\implies\theta_{\ell}\leq 4/3\exp(-2^{\ell-\ell_{0}}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem8.p2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem8.p2.3.1" class="ltx_text">Setting this <math id="Thmtheorem8.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="&lt;\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">&lt;\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math> gives the claim.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS1.p16" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS1.p16.1" class="ltx_p">We again note that this <math id="A5.SS1.p16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa_{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>κ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa_{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math> is the square of the condition number of <math id="A5.SS1.p16.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math> - however, this distinction is easily accommodated due to the logarithmic dependence on it - the only change is that the <math id="A5.SS1.p16.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3/5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3/5</annotation></semantics></math> above increases to <math id="A5.SS1.p16.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="6/5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">6/5</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS1.p17" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS1.p17.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="A5.SS1.p17.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic"><span id="A5.SS1.p17.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Back to <math id="A5.SS1.p17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">N</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math></span>. </em> The conditioning of <math id="A5.SS1.p17.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math> yields a direct control on the behaviour of <math id="A5.SS1.p17.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>N</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math>, as encapsulated below. We note that if <math id="A5.SS1.p17.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> is not full rank, the statement holds for <math id="A5.SS1.p17.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{N}_{\ell}=(I-P_{0})N_{\ell}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>N</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{N}_{\ell}=(I-P_{0})N_{\ell},</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="A5.SS1.p17.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> projects onto the kernel of <math id="A5.SS1.p17.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem9" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem9.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 9</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem9.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem9.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmtheorem9.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem9.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For all <math id="Thmtheorem9.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\ell,\|N_{\ell}\|_{2}\leq\exp(-\sum_{l&lt;\ell}\gamma_{l}\underline{\lambda}_{l}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.0835em">≤</mo><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.055em">−</mo><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><msub><munder accentunder="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell,\|N_{\ell}\|_{2}\leq\exp(-\sum_{l&lt;\ell}\gamma_{l}\underline{\lambda}_{l}</annotation></semantics></math>. Further, if <math id="Thmtheorem9.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\forall\ell,\eta_{\ell}=\overline{\lambda}^{-1}/3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\forall\ell,\eta_{\ell}=\overline{\lambda}^{-1}/3</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmtheorem9.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{\ell}=\overline{\lambda}^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{\ell}=\overline{\lambda}^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="Thmtheorem9.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|N_{\ell}\|_{2}\leq\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|N_{\ell}\|_{2}\leq\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="Thmtheorem9.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell\geq L+1," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell\geq L+1,</annotation></semantics></math> where</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex75" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex75.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="L=2+\lceil 3/5\log(\kappa_{0})\rceil+\lceil\log_{2}(\log 4/3\varepsilon))\rceil." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌈</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>5</mn><mi>log</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>κ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌉</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌈</mo><msub><mi>log</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>log</mi><mn>4</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌉</mo><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L=2+\lceil 3/5\log(\kappa_{0})\rceil+\lceil\log_{2}(\log 4/3\varepsilon))\rceil.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem9.4" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem9.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmtheorem9.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem9.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="Thmtheorem9.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{l+1}=(I-\gamma_{l}\mathcal{E}_{l})N_{l}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{l+1}=(I-\gamma_{l}\mathcal{E}_{l})N_{l},</annotation></semantics></math> we immediately have</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex76" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex76.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|N_{\ell}\|_{2}\leq\prod_{l&lt;\ell}\|I-\gamma_{l}\mathcal{E}_{l}\|_{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">≤</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∏</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></munder><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|N_{\ell}\|_{2}\leq\prod_{l&lt;\ell}\|I-\gamma_{l}\mathcal{E}_{l}\|_{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem9.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem9.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">But note that <math id="Thmtheorem9.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|I-\gamma_{l}\mathcal{E}_{l}\|_{2}=(1-\gamma_{l}\underline{\lambda}_{l})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><munder accentunder="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|I-\gamma_{l}\mathcal{E}_{l}\|_{2}=(1-\gamma_{l}\underline{\lambda}_{l})</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus, we immediately have <math id="Thmtheorem9.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|N_{\ell}\|\leq\prod(1-\gamma_{l}\underline{\lambda}_{l})\leq\exp(\sum_{l&lt;\ell}\gamma_{l}\underline{\lambda}_{l})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">≤</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">∏</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><munder accentunder="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><munder accentunder="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|N_{\ell}\|\leq\prod(1-\gamma_{l}\underline{\lambda}_{l})\leq\exp(\sum_{l&lt;\ell}\gamma_{l}\underline{\lambda}_{l})</annotation></semantics></math>.
Further, recall from Lemma <a href="#Thmtheorem8" title="Lemma 8. ‣ E.1 Analysis of the Unconstrained or Centralized Iteration ‣ Appendix E Theoretical Analyses ‣ Linear Transformers Implicitly DiscoverUnified Numerical Algorithms" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a> that if <math id="Thmtheorem9.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta_{\ell}=\overline{\lambda}^{-1}/3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta_{\ell}=\overline{\lambda}^{-1}/3</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="Thmtheorem9.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell,</annotation></semantics></math> then <math id="Thmtheorem9.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{\lambda}_{\ell}\geq\overline{\lambda}_{\ell}/(1+\varepsilon)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><munder accentunder="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{\lambda}_{\ell}\geq\overline{\lambda}_{\ell}/(1+\varepsilon)</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="Thmtheorem9.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell\geq L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>≥</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell\geq L</annotation></semantics></math>. But then, if <math id="Thmtheorem9.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta_{\ell}=\overline{\lambda}^{-1}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta_{\ell}=\overline{\lambda}^{-1},</annotation></semantics></math> we have</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex77" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex77.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\eta_{\ell}\underline{\lambda}\leq 1-\underline{\lambda}/\overline{\lambda}\leq\varepsilon/(1+\varepsilon)\leq\varepsilon," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><munder accentunder="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><munder accentunder="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mo>/</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\eta_{\ell}\underline{\lambda}\leq 1-\underline{\lambda}/\overline{\lambda}\leq\varepsilon/(1+\varepsilon)\leq\varepsilon,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem9.p2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem9.p2.3.1" class="ltx_text">yielding the claimed bound on <math id="Thmtheorem9.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|N_{\ell}\|_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|N_{\ell}\|_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS1.p18" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS1.p18.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="A5.SS1.p18.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_bold ltx_font_italic">Finishing the Error Control.</em> With all the pieces in place, we conclude the main argument.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 1. ‣ 5.1 Unconstrained (centralized) setting ‣ 5 Evaluation of EAGLE ‣ Linear Transformers Implicitly DiscoverUnified Numerical Algorithms" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="A5.SS1.p19" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS1.p19.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS1.p19.1.1" class="ltx_text">By Lemma <a href="#Thmtheorem4" title="Lemma 4. ‣ E.1 Analysis of the Unconstrained or Centralized Iteration ‣ Appendix E Theoretical Analyses ‣ Linear Transformers Implicitly DiscoverUnified Numerical Algorithms" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>, we have <math id="A5.SS1.p19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{\ell}-\hat{D}_{*}=W_{*}N_{\ell}C_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>D</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>∗</mo></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\ell}-\hat{D}_{*}=W_{*}N_{\ell}C_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>, and consequently,</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex78" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex78.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|D_{\ell}-\hat{D}_{*}\|_{F}\leq\|W_{*}N_{\ell}\|_{F}\|C_{0}\|_{F}\leq\sqrt{\mathrm{rank}(W_{*}N_{\ell})}\|W_{*}N_{\ell}\|_{2}\|C_{0}\|_{F}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>D</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>∗</mo></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mi>rank</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|D_{\ell}-\hat{D}_{*}\|_{F}\leq\|W_{*}N_{\ell}\|_{F}\|C_{0}\|_{F}\leq\sqrt{\mathrm{rank}(W_{*}N_{\ell})}\|W_{*}N_{\ell}\|_{2}\|C_{0}\|_{F}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.p19.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS1.p19.2.1" class="ltx_text">But, since <math id="A5.SS1.p19.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{*}N_{\ell}\in\mathbb{R}^{d^{\prime}\times d}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{*}N_{\ell}\in\mathbb{R}^{d^{\prime}\times d},</annotation></semantics></math> the rank about is at most <math id="A5.SS1.p19.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>. Finally, <math id="A5.SS1.p19.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|W_{*}N_{\ell}\|_{2}\leq\|N_{\ell}\|_{2}\|W_{*}\|_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|W_{*}N_{\ell}\|_{2}\leq\|N_{\ell}\|_{2}\|W_{*}\|_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus, the claim follows as soon as <math id="A5.SS1.p19.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|N_{\ell}\|_{2}\leq\varepsilon/(\sqrt{d^{\prime}}\|W_{*}\|_{2}\|C_{0}\|_{F})," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msqrt><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|N_{\ell}\|_{2}\leq\varepsilon/(\sqrt{d^{\prime}}\|W_{*}\|_{2}\|C_{0}\|_{F}),</annotation></semantics></math> for which we may invoke Lemma <a href="#Thmtheorem9" title="Lemma 9. ‣ E.1 Analysis of the Unconstrained or Centralized Iteration ‣ Appendix E Theoretical Analyses ‣ Linear Transformers Implicitly DiscoverUnified Numerical Algorithms" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS1.p20" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS1.p20.1" class="ltx_p">Again, recall that for the purposes of error, if <math id="A5.SS1.p20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> were not full rank, then we could instead replace <math id="A5.SS1.p20.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>N</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math> by <math id="A5.SS1.p20.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{N}_{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>N</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{N}_{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math> in all statements above, and thus the claim also extends to this situation.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS1.p21" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS1.p21.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="A5.SS1.p21.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_bold ltx_font_italic">Comment on Rates <math id="A5.SS1.p21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta,\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">η</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">γ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta,\gamma</annotation></semantics></math>.</em> Going back to the notation of Algorithm <a href="#algofigure1" title="List of algofigures 1 ‣ 4 Emergent Algorithm ‣ Linear Transformers Implicitly DiscoverUnified Numerical Algorithms" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, we reparametrise <math id="A5.SS1.p21.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{\ell}=\rho_{\ell}=\overline{\lambda}_{\ell}^{-1}=\|A_{\ell}\|_{2}^{-2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{\ell}=\rho_{\ell}=\overline{\lambda}_{\ell}^{-1}=\|A_{\ell}\|_{2}^{-2}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A5.SS1.p21.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta_{\ell}=\rho_{\ell}/3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta_{\ell}=\rho_{\ell}/3</annotation></semantics></math>. It is worth discussing briefly how we may go about estimating this <math id="A5.SS1.p21.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS1.p22" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS1.p22.1" class="ltx_p">A simple observation in this setting is that if we assume that we know <math id="A5.SS1.p22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{\lambda}_{0}=\|\mathcal{E}_{0}\|_{0}=\|A\|_{2}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{\lambda}_{0}=\|\mathcal{E}_{0}\|_{0}=\|A\|_{2}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> to begin with, then it is a simple matter to compute the subsequent values of <math id="A5.SS1.p22.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{\lambda}_{\ell}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{\lambda}_{\ell},</annotation></semantics></math> since if we set <math id="A5.SS1.p22.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta_{\ell},\gamma_{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta_{\ell},\gamma_{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math> as per the above, this is directly computed iteratively via</p>
<table id="A5.Ex79" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex79.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{\lambda}_{\ell+1}=\overline{\lambda}_{\ell}(1-1/3)^{2}=4\overline{\lambda}_{\ell}/9." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>9</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{\lambda}_{\ell+1}=\overline{\lambda}_{\ell}(1-1/3)^{2}=4\overline{\lambda}_{\ell}/9.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.p22.2" class="ltx_p">In fact, under this assumption, we may avoid further numerical stability issues by first recaling <math id="A5.SS1.p22.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> to have <math id="A5.SS1.p22.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2</annotation></semantics></math>-norm <math id="A5.SS1.p22.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>, and subsequently simply rescaling the matrices up <math id="A5.SS1.p22.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{\ell},B_{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{\ell},B_{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math> by <math id="A5.SS1.p22.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3/2</annotation></semantics></math> after each update to maintain the invariant <math id="A5.SS1.p22.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{\lambda}_{\ell}=\overline{\lambda}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{\lambda}_{\ell}=\overline{\lambda}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>—the behaviour of <math id="A5.SS1.p22.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>N</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math> remains the same, and convergence rates are only driven by the conditioning of <math id="A5.SS1.p22.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math>. So, equivalently, the question we must concern ourselves with is finding <math id="A5.SS1.p22.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|A\|_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|A\|_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. Of course, this is quite cheap, since we can compute this simply by power iteration, which involves only matrix-vector products rather than matrix-matrix products. Nevertheless, note that power iteration is only linearly convergent (i.e., the number of iterations needed to find a <math id="A5.SS1.p22.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ε</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math>-approximation of the top eigenvalue is <math id="A5.SS1.p22.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Theta(\log(1/\varepsilon)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">CLOSE</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Theta(\log(1/\varepsilon)</annotation></semantics></math>), so in full generality, this procedure would destroy the second order convergence.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS1.p23" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS1.p23.1" class="ltx_p">In our simulations of §<a href="#S5" title="5 Evaluation of EAGLE ‣ Linear Transformers Implicitly DiscoverUnified Numerical Algorithms" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>, we indeed implemented these iterations by carrying out power iteration. Note that practically, then, the method essentially retains its second order behaviour despite this approximation. One aspect of this lies in the fact that even if we underestimate the top eigenvalue by a small amount, and so undertune <math id="A5.SS1.p23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta,\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta,\gamma</annotation></semantics></math> by a slight amount, the second order bound of Lemma <a href="#Thmtheorem8" title="Lemma 8. ‣ E.1 Analysis of the Unconstrained or Centralized Iteration ‣ Appendix E Theoretical Analyses ‣ Linear Transformers Implicitly DiscoverUnified Numerical Algorithms" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a> decays gracefully, and so retains practical resilience. Of course, characterising exactly how loose this can be requires more precise analysis, which we leave for future work.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A5.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">E.2 </span>Distributed Analysis</h3>

<div id="A5.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Beginning again with Algorithm <a href="#algofigure1" title="List of algofigures 1 ‣ 4 Emergent Algorithm ‣ Linear Transformers Implicitly DiscoverUnified Numerical Algorithms" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, with <math id="A5.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S=I_{n},M&gt;1," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S=I_{n},M&gt;1,</annotation></semantics></math> we need to analyse the iterations</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="A5.EGx11" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.E7"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\forall\mu,A_{\ell+1}^{\mu}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>μ</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\forall\mu,A_{\ell+1}^{\mu}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=A_{\ell}^{\mu}(I-\eta_{\ell}^{\mu}A_{\ell}^{\mu,\top}A_{\ell}^{\mu})," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>μ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>η</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>μ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em">⊤</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>μ</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=A_{\ell}^{\mu}(I-\eta_{\ell}^{\mu}A_{\ell}^{\mu,\top}A_{\ell}^{\mu}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(7)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex80"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex80.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\forall\mu,B_{\ell+1}^{\mu}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>μ</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\forall\mu,B_{\ell+1}^{\mu}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex80.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=B_{\ell}^{\mu}(I-\eta_{\ell}^{\mu}A_{\ell}^{\mu,\top}A_{\ell}^{\mu})," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>μ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>η</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>μ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em">⊤</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>μ</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=B_{\ell}^{\mu}(I-\eta_{\ell}^{\mu}A_{\ell}^{\mu,\top}A_{\ell}^{\mu}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex81"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex81.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle C_{\ell+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle C_{\ell+1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex81.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=C_{\ell}-\frac{1}{m}\sum_{\mu}\gamma_{\ell}A_{\ell}^{\mu}A_{\ell}^{\mu,\top}C_{\ell}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>m</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>μ</mi></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>μ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em">⊤</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=C_{\ell}-\frac{1}{m}\sum_{\mu}\gamma_{\ell}A_{\ell}^{\mu}A_{\ell}^{\mu,\top}C_{\ell},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex82"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex82.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle D_{\ell+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle D_{\ell+1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex82.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=D_{\ell}+\frac{1}{m}\sum_{\mu}\gamma_{\ell}B_{\ell}^{\mu}A_{\ell}^{\mu,\top}C_{\ell}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>m</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>μ</mi></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>μ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em">⊤</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=D_{\ell}+\frac{1}{m}\sum_{\mu}\gamma_{\ell}B_{\ell}^{\mu}A_{\ell}^{\mu,\top}C_{\ell}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We note that here we have set <math id="A5.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math> to be constant across all machines, and nominally it is not pegged to <math id="A5.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|A_{\ell}^{\mu}\|_{2}^{-2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>μ</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|A_{\ell}^{\mu}\|_{2}^{-2}</annotation></semantics></math>, which could vary across machines. However, we will analyze this method under the normalization assumption that</p>
<table id="A5.Ex83" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex83.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\forall\mu,\|A_{0}^{\mu}\|_{2}=1." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>μ</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\forall\mu,\|A_{0}^{\mu}\|_{2}=1.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.p2.2" class="ltx_p">In this setting, we will show that the choices <math id="A5.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta_{\ell}^{\mu}=\|A_{\ell}^{\mu}\|_{2}^{-2}/3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>η</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>μ</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>μ</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta_{\ell}^{\mu}=\|A_{\ell}^{\mu}\|_{2}^{-2}/3</annotation></semantics></math> are also the same for each machine, and then set <math id="A5.SS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{\ell}=3\eta_{\ell}^{\mu}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>η</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>μ</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{\ell}=3\eta_{\ell}^{\mu}</annotation></semantics></math> (which in turn is also the same for every machine). Thus, in the setting we analyze, the iterations above are faitful to the structure of Algorithm <a href="#algofigure1" title="List of algofigures 1 ‣ 4 Emergent Algorithm ‣ Linear Transformers Implicitly DiscoverUnified Numerical Algorithms" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Note, of course, that this distributed data computes the Nyström approximation of</p>
<table id="A5.Ex84" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex84.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{bmatrix}A&amp;C\\
B&amp;D\end{bmatrix}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mi>A</mi></mtd><mtd><mi>C</mi></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mi>B</mi></mtd><mtd><mi>D</mi></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{bmatrix}A&amp;C\\
B&amp;D\end{bmatrix},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.p3.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A5.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C,D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C,D</annotation></semantics></math> are as in the iteration, while</p>
<table id="A5.Ex85" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex85.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A=\begin{bmatrix}A^{1}&amp;A^{2}&amp;\cdots&amp;A^{m}\end{bmatrix},B=\begin{bmatrix}B^{1}&amp;B^{2}&amp;\cdots&amp;B^{m}\end{bmatrix}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true"><mtr><mtd><msup><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></mtd><mtd><msup><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mtd><mtd><mo>⋯</mo></mtd><mtd><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>m</mi></msup></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true"><mtr><mtd><msup><mi>B</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></mtd><mtd><msup><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mtd><mtd><mo>⋯</mo></mtd><mtd><msup><mi>B</mi><mi>m</mi></msup></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A=\begin{bmatrix}A^{1}&amp;A^{2}&amp;\cdots&amp;A^{m}\end{bmatrix},B=\begin{bmatrix}B^{1}&amp;B^{2}&amp;\cdots&amp;B^{m}\end{bmatrix}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">We will work in the noise-free regime, wherein there exists a matrix <math id="A5.SS2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{*}</annotation></semantics></math> such that</p>
<table id="A5.Ex86" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex86.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{bmatrix}B&amp;D\end{bmatrix}=W_{*}\begin{bmatrix}A&amp;C\end{bmatrix}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true"><mtr><mtd><mi>B</mi></mtd><mtd><mi>D</mi></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true"><mtr><mtd><mi>A</mi></mtd><mtd><mi>C</mi></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{bmatrix}B&amp;D\end{bmatrix}=W_{*}\begin{bmatrix}A&amp;C\end{bmatrix},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.p4.2" class="ltx_p">and <math id="A5.SS2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C\in\operatorname{column-span}(A)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>column</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>span</mi></mrow><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C\in\operatorname{column-span}(A)</annotation></semantics></math>. Of course, this <math id="A5.SS2.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{*}</annotation></semantics></math> also equals the Nyström parameter for this matrix (§<a href="#A1.SS1" title="A.1 Nyström Approximation ‣ Appendix A Methodological Details ‣ Linear Transformers Implicitly DiscoverUnified Numerical Algorithms" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.1</span></a>). The second condition ensures that the rank of this matrix is the same as that of <math id="A5.SS2.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>, and is needed to ensure that we can actually infer <math id="A5.SS2.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{*}</annotation></semantics></math> in the directions constituted by the columns of <math id="A5.SS2.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> (without which one cannot recover <math id="A5.SS2.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math>).</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS2.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS2.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="A5.SS2.p5.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_bold ltx_font_italic">Per-machine and Global Signal Energies</em><span id="A5.SS2.p5.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span> We being with defining the energy and correlation matrices in analogy to the previous section. As before, <math id="A5.SS2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{\mu}_{0}=A^{\mu},B^{\mu}_{0}=B^{\mu},C_{0}=C,D_{0}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>μ</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>μ</mi></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>μ</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>B</mi><mi>μ</mi></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{\mu}_{0}=A^{\mu},B^{\mu}_{0}=B^{\mu},C_{0}=C,D_{0}=0</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmdefinition4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmdefinition4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 4</span></span><span id="Thmdefinition4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmdefinition4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmdefinition4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We define the per-machine objects</p>
<table id="A5.Ex87" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex87.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}^{\mu}_{\ell}:=A_{\ell}^{\mu}A_{\ell}^{\mu,\top}\textit{ and }\mathcal{V}^{\mu}_{\ell}:=B_{\ell}^{\mu}A_{\ell}^{\mu,\top}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>μ</mi></msubsup><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>μ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em">⊤</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic"> and </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>μ</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>μ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em">⊤</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}^{\mu}_{\ell}:=A_{\ell}^{\mu}A_{\ell}^{\mu,\top}\textit{ and }\mathcal{V}^{\mu}_{\ell}:=B_{\ell}^{\mu}A_{\ell}^{\mu,\top},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmdefinition4.p1.2" class="ltx_p">and the per-machine values</p>
<table id="A5.Ex88" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex88.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{\lambda}_{\ell}^{\mu}=\lambda^{1}(\mathcal{E}_{\ell}^{\mu}),\underline{\lambda}_{\ell}^{\mu}=\lambda^{r(\mu)}(\mathcal{E}_{\ell}^{\mu})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>μ</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>λ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>μ</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><munder accentunder="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>μ</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>μ</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{\lambda}_{\ell}^{\mu}=\lambda^{1}(\mathcal{E}_{\ell}^{\mu}),\underline{\lambda}_{\ell}^{\mu}=\lambda^{r(\mu)}(\mathcal{E}_{\ell}^{\mu}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmdefinition4.p1.3" class="ltx_p">where <math id="Thmdefinition4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r(\mu)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r(\mu)</annotation></semantics></math> is the rank of <math id="Thmdefinition4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{0}^{\mu}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>μ</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{0}^{\mu}</annotation></semantics></math>. Further, we define the global signal energy</p>
<table id="A5.Ex89" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex89.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{\mathcal{E}}_{\ell}:=\frac{1}{m}\sum\mathcal{E}_{\ell}^{\mu}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>m</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>μ</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{\mathcal{E}}_{\ell}:=\frac{1}{m}\sum\mathcal{E}_{\ell}^{\mu}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS2.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS2.p6.1" class="ltx_p">Note that by our assumption, <math id="A5.SS2.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\mathcal{E}_{0}^{\mu}\|_{2}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>μ</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\mathcal{E}_{0}^{\mu}\|_{2}=1</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A5.SS2.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math>. Further, the behaviour of <math id="A5.SS2.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}^{\mu}_{\ell},\mathcal{V}^{\mu}_{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>μ</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>μ</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}^{\mu}_{\ell},\mathcal{V}^{\mu}_{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math> is identical to that in the centralised case, i.e.,</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem10" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem10.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 10</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem10.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem10.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmtheorem10.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem10.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For all <math id="Thmtheorem10.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu,\ell," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu,\ell,</annotation></semantics></math></span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex90" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex90.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}^{\mu}_{\ell+1}=\mathcal{E}^{\mu}_{\ell}(I-\eta_{\ell}^{\mu}\mathcal{E}^{\mu}_{\ell})^{2}\textit{ and }\mathcal{V}^{\mu}_{\ell+1}=\mathcal{V}^{\mu}_{\ell}(I-\eta_{\ell}^{\mu}\mathcal{E}^{\mu}_{\ell})^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>μ</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>μ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>η</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>μ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>μ</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic"> and </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>μ</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>μ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>η</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>μ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>μ</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}^{\mu}_{\ell+1}=\mathcal{E}^{\mu}_{\ell}(I-\eta_{\ell}^{\mu}\mathcal{E}^{\mu}_{\ell})^{2}\textit{ and }\mathcal{V}^{\mu}_{\ell+1}=\mathcal{V}^{\mu}_{\ell}(I-\eta_{\ell}^{\mu}\mathcal{E}^{\mu}_{\ell})^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem10.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem10.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">As a consequence, for every <math id="Thmtheorem10.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell,\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell,\mu</annotation></semantics></math>, it holds that</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex91" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex91.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}^{\mu}_{\ell}=W_{*}\mathcal{E}^{\mu}_{\ell}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>μ</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>μ</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}^{\mu}_{\ell}=W_{*}\mathcal{E}^{\mu}_{\ell}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem10.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem10.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Finally, for any <math id="Thmtheorem10.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell,</annotation></semantics></math></span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex92" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex92.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{\ell+1}=(I-\gamma_{\ell}\overline{\mathcal{E}}_{\ell})C_{\ell}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{\ell+1}=(I-\gamma_{\ell}\overline{\mathcal{E}}_{\ell})C_{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem10.4" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem10.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmtheorem10.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem10.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">The iterations for <math id="Thmtheorem10.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}^{\mu}_{\ell+1},\mathcal{V}^{\mu}_{\ell+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>μ</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>μ</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}^{\mu}_{\ell+1},\mathcal{V}^{\mu}_{\ell+1}</annotation></semantics></math> follow identically to the proof of Lemma <a href="#Thmtheorem3" title="Lemma 3. ‣ E.1 Analysis of the Unconstrained or Centralized Iteration ‣ Appendix E Theoretical Analyses ‣ Linear Transformers Implicitly DiscoverUnified Numerical Algorithms" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>. For the second claim, notice that we have</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex93" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex93.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B^{\mu}=W_{*}A^{\mu}\implies\mathcal{V}_{0}^{\mu}=W_{*}\mathcal{E}_{0}^{\mu}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>B</mi><mi>μ</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>μ</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟹</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>μ</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>μ</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B^{\mu}=W_{*}A^{\mu}\implies\mathcal{V}_{0}^{\mu}=W_{*}\mathcal{E}_{0}^{\mu}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem10.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem10.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">by multiplying by <math id="Thmtheorem10.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{\mu,\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em">⊤</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{\mu,\top}</annotation></semantics></math> on both sides. Then the claimed invariance follows inductively.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem10.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmtheorem10.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem10.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">Finally, noting that <math id="Thmtheorem10.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}^{\mu}_{\ell}=A_{\ell}^{\mu}A_{\ell}^{\mu,\top}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>μ</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>μ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em">⊤</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}^{\mu}_{\ell}=A_{\ell}^{\mu}A_{\ell}^{\mu,\top},</annotation></semantics></math> we immediately have</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex94" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex94.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="C_{\ell+1}=\left(I-\gamma_{\ell}\cdot\frac{1}{m}\sum_{\mu}\mathcal{E}^{\mu}_{\ell}\right)C_{\ell}=(I-\gamma_{\ell}\overline{\mathcal{E}}_{\ell})C_{\ell}\qed" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>m</mi></mfrac><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>μ</mi></munder><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>μ</mi></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo class="ltx_mathvariant_italic" lspace="0em" mathvariant="italic" separator="true">∎</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{\ell+1}=\left(I-\gamma_{\ell}\cdot\frac{1}{m}\sum_{\mu}\mathcal{E}^{\mu}_{\ell}\right)C_{\ell}=(I-\gamma_{\ell}\overline{\mathcal{E}}_{\ell})C_{\ell}\qed</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS2.p7" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS2.p7.1" class="ltx_p">In analogy with the centralized case, this leads us to define the following matrices.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmdefinition5" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmdefinition5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 5</span></span><span id="Thmdefinition5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmdefinition5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmdefinition5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We define</p>
<table id="A5.Ex95" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex95.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{\ell}^{\mu}=\prod_{l&lt;\ell}(I-\eta_{\ell}^{\mu}\mathcal{E}_{\ell}^{\mu})^{2}\textit{ and }N_{\ell}^{\top}:=\prod_{l&lt;\ell}(I-\gamma_{\ell}\overline{\mathcal{E}}_{\ell})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>μ</mi></msubsup><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∏</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>η</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>μ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>μ</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic"> and </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>N</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">:=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∏</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{\ell}^{\mu}=\prod_{l&lt;\ell}(I-\eta_{\ell}^{\mu}\mathcal{E}_{\ell}^{\mu})^{2}\textit{ and }N_{\ell}^{\top}:=\prod_{l&lt;\ell}(I-\gamma_{\ell}\overline{\mathcal{E}}_{\ell}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmdefinition5.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where again <math id="Thmdefinition5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\prod" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>∏</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\prod</annotation></semantics></math> is interpreted as multiplication from the right, and <math id="Thmdefinition5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{0}^{\mu}=N_{0}=I_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>μ</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{0}^{\mu}=N_{0}=I_{d}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS2.p8" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS2.p8.1" class="ltx_p">Succinctly, then, we can write <math id="A5.SS2.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}^{\mu}_{\ell}=\mathcal{E}_{0}^{\mu}M_{\ell}^{\mu}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>μ</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>μ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>μ</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}^{\mu}_{\ell}=\mathcal{E}_{0}^{\mu}M_{\ell}^{\mu}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.SS2.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{\ell}=N_{\ell}C_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{\ell}=N_{\ell}C_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS2.p9" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS2.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="A5.SS2.p9.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_bold ltx_font_italic">Telescoping the Error.</em> This notation allows us to set up the following analogue of Lemma <a href="#Thmtheorem4" title="Lemma 4. ‣ E.1 Analysis of the Unconstrained or Centralized Iteration ‣ Appendix E Theoretical Analyses ‣ Linear Transformers Implicitly DiscoverUnified Numerical Algorithms" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem11" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem11.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 11</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem11.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem11.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmtheorem11.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem11.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Under the distributed iterations without noise, it holds for all <math id="Thmtheorem11.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell</annotation></semantics></math> that</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex96" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex96.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{\ell}=W_{*}(I-N_{\ell})C_{0}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\ell}=W_{*}(I-N_{\ell})C_{0}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem11.4" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem11.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmtheorem11.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem11.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Observe that</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex97" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex97.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{\ell}=\sum_{l&lt;\ell}\gamma_{l}\cdot\sum_{\mu}\frac{\mathcal{V}_{l}^{\mu}}{m}C_{l}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></munder><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.055em">⋅</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>μ</mi></munder><mrow><mfrac><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>l</mi><mi>μ</mi></msubsup><mi>m</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\ell}=\sum_{l&lt;\ell}\gamma_{l}\cdot\sum_{\mu}\frac{\mathcal{V}_{l}^{\mu}}{m}C_{l}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem11.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem11.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">Now, <math id="Thmtheorem11.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}_{l}^{\mu}=W_{*}\mathcal{E}_{l}^{\mu}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>l</mi><mi>μ</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>l</mi><mi>μ</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}_{l}^{\mu}=W_{*}\mathcal{E}_{l}^{\mu},</annotation></semantics></math> and so</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex98" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex98.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\frac{1}{m}\sum_{\mu}\mathcal{V}_{l}^{\mu}=W_{*}\cdot\frac{1}{m}\sum_{\mu}\mathcal{E}_{l}^{\mu}=W_{*}\overline{\mathcal{E}}_{l}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>m</mi></mfrac><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>μ</mi></msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>l</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>μ</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>W</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>m</mi></mfrac><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>μ</mi></msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>l</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>μ</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>W</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{m}\sum_{\mu}\mathcal{V}_{l}^{\mu}=W_{*}\cdot\frac{1}{m}\sum_{\mu}\mathcal{E}_{l}^{\mu}=W_{*}\overline{\mathcal{E}}_{l}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem11.p2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem11.p2.3.1" class="ltx_text">Thus, we have</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex99" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex99.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{\ell}=W_{*}\left(\sum_{l&lt;\ell}\gamma_{l}\overline{\mathcal{E}}_{l}N_{l}\right)C_{0}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\ell}=W_{*}\left(\sum_{l&lt;\ell}\gamma_{l}\overline{\mathcal{E}}_{l}N_{l}\right)C_{0}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem11.p2.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem11.p2.4.1" class="ltx_text">But</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex100" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex100.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{l+1}=(I-\gamma_{l}\mathcal{E}_{l})N_{l}\iff\gamma_{l}\overline{\mathcal{E}}_{l}N_{l}=N_{l}-N_{l+1}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⇔</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{l+1}=(I-\gamma_{l}\mathcal{E}_{l})N_{l}\iff\gamma_{l}\overline{\mathcal{E}}_{l}N_{l}=N_{l}-N_{l+1},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem11.p2.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem11.p2.5.1" class="ltx_text">and so the term in the brackets telescopes to <math id="Thmtheorem11.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{0}-N_{\ell}=I-N_{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{0}-N_{\ell}=I-N_{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS2.p10" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS2.p10.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="A5.SS2.p10.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_bold ltx_font_italic">Conditioning</em><span id="A5.SS2.p10.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span> Of course, again, <math id="A5.SS2.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D=W_{*}C=W_{*}(I)C_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D=W_{*}C=W_{*}(I)C_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>. So, to gain error control, we only need to argue (as before) that <math id="A5.SS2.p10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|N_{\ell}\|_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|N_{\ell}\|_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> vanishes quickly with <math id="A5.SS2.p10.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell</annotation></semantics></math>. As before, this relies strongly on the condition number of <math id="A5.SS2.p10.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{\mathcal{E}}_{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{\mathcal{E}}_{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math>. We note, again, that we will simply assume that <math id="A5.SS2.p10.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{\mathcal{E}}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{\mathcal{E}}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> is full-rank, since rank-deficiency is rendered moot in this case by the fact that <math id="A5.SS2.p10.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> lies in the column span of <math id="A5.SS2.p10.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> (and hence, is orthogonal to the kernel of <math id="A5.SS2.p10.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{\mathcal{E}}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{\mathcal{E}}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>). However, the individual <math id="A5.SS2.p10.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}^{\mu}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>μ</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}^{\mu}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> may not be full rank, and so the distinction between <math id="A5.SS2.p10.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{\lambda}(\mathcal{E}^{\mu})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder accentunder="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>μ</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{\lambda}(\mathcal{E}^{\mu})</annotation></semantics></math> and the smallest eigenvalue of <math id="A5.SS2.p10.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}^{\mu}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>μ</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}^{\mu}</annotation></semantics></math> (which is usually <math id="A5.SS2.p10.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math>) should not be forgotten, although it will not matter very much for our expressions.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS2.p11" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS2.p11.1" class="ltx_p">To begin with, we note that since the per-machine <math id="A5.SS2.p11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{\mu},B^{\mu}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>μ</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>B</mi><mi>μ</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{\mu},B^{\mu}</annotation></semantics></math> iterations are identical to the central case, the corresponding <math id="A5.SS2.p11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}^{\mu}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>μ</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}^{\mu}</annotation></semantics></math> are conditioned at the same quadratic rate we saw previously. We formally state this below.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem12" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem12.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 12</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem12.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem12.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmtheorem12.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem12.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For all <math id="Thmtheorem12.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell,</annotation></semantics></math> set <math id="Thmtheorem12.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta_{\ell}^{\mu}:=(\overline{\lambda}^{\mu}_{\ell})^{-1}/3," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>η</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>μ</mi></msubsup><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>μ</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta_{\ell}^{\mu}:=(\overline{\lambda}^{\mu}_{\ell})^{-1}/3,</annotation></semantics></math> and define <math id="Thmtheorem12.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa_{\ell}^{\mu}=\overline{\lambda}_{\ell}^{\mu}/\underline{\lambda}_{\ell}^{\mu}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>κ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>μ</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>μ</mi></msubsup><mo>/</mo><msubsup><munder accentunder="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>μ</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa_{\ell}^{\mu}=\overline{\lambda}_{\ell}^{\mu}/\underline{\lambda}_{\ell}^{\mu}.</annotation></semantics></math></span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex101" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex101.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textit{If }\ell\geq L(\varepsilon):=2+\lceil 3/5\log(\max_{\mu}\kappa_{0}^{\mu})\rceil+\lceil\log_{2}(\log(4/3\varepsilon))\rceil,\textit{ then }\max_{\mu}\kappa_{\ell}^{\mu}\leq 1+\varepsilon." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">If </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌈</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mi>μ</mi></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msubsup><mi>κ</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>μ</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌉</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>log</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌉</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic"> then </mtext><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><munder><mi>max</mi><mi>μ</mi></munder><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>κ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>μ</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textit{If }\ell\geq L(\varepsilon):=2+\lceil 3/5\log(\max_{\mu}\kappa_{0}^{\mu})\rceil+\lceil\log_{2}(\log(4/3\varepsilon))\rceil,\textit{ then }\max_{\mu}\kappa_{\ell}^{\mu}\leq 1+\varepsilon.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem12.4" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem12.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem12.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem12.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Apply Lemma <a href="#Thmtheorem8" title="Lemma 8. ‣ E.1 Analysis of the Unconstrained or Centralized Iteration ‣ Appendix E Theoretical Analyses ‣ Linear Transformers Implicitly DiscoverUnified Numerical Algorithms" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS2.p12" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS2.p12.1" class="ltx_p">Of course, <math id="A5.SS2.p12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{\mathcal{E}}_{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{\mathcal{E}}_{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math>, as an average, will not have the same conditioning behaviour. In fact, this is strongly sensitive to the diversity index <math id="A5.SS2.p12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> from Definition <a href="#Thmdefinition1" title="Definition 1. ‣ 5.2 Distributed setting ‣ 5 Evaluation of EAGLE ‣ Linear Transformers Implicitly DiscoverUnified Numerical Algorithms" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, as captured below.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem13" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem13.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 13</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem13.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem13.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmtheorem13.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem13.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Suppose that <math id="Thmtheorem13.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{0}^{\mu}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>μ</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{0}^{\mu}</annotation></semantics></math> is constant across machines, and for all <math id="Thmtheorem13.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu,\ell,\eta_{\ell}^{\mu}=(\overline{\lambda}^{\mu}_{\ell})^{-1}/3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>η</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>μ</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>μ</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu,\ell,\eta_{\ell}^{\mu}=(\overline{\lambda}^{\mu}_{\ell})^{-1}/3</annotation></semantics></math>. Define</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex102" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex102.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{\kappa}_{\ell}=\overline{\lambda}(\overline{\mathcal{E}}_{\ell})/\underline{\lambda}(\overline{\mathcal{E}}_{\ell})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>κ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><munder accentunder="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{\kappa}_{\ell}=\overline{\lambda}(\overline{\mathcal{E}}_{\ell})/\underline{\lambda}(\overline{\mathcal{E}}_{\ell}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="A5.Ex103" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex103.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textit{If }\ell\geq L(\varepsilon),\textit{ then }\overline{\kappa}_{\ell}\leq\frac{1+\varepsilon}{\alpha}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">If </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic"> then </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>κ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mi>α</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textit{If }\ell\geq L(\varepsilon),\textit{ then }\overline{\kappa}_{\ell}\leq\frac{1+\varepsilon}{\alpha},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem13.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem13.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="Thmtheorem13.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L(\varepsilon)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L(\varepsilon)</annotation></semantics></math> is the expression in Lemma <a href="#Thmtheorem12" title="Lemma 12. ‣ E.2 Distributed Analysis ‣ Appendix E Theoretical Analyses ‣ Linear Transformers Implicitly DiscoverUnified Numerical Algorithms" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">12</span></a>. Further, for the same range of <math id="Thmtheorem13.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell,</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="Thmtheorem13.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex104" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex104.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{\lambda}(\overline{\mathcal{E}}_{\ell})\geq\frac{\overline{\lambda}^{\mu}_{\ell}\cdot\alpha}{1+\varepsilon}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder accentunder="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>μ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{\lambda}(\overline{\mathcal{E}}_{\ell})\geq\frac{\overline{\lambda}^{\mu}_{\ell}\cdot\alpha}{1+\varepsilon}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem13.4" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem13.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmtheorem13.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem13.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Firstly, by Weyl’s inequality, notice that</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex105" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex105.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{\lambda}(\overline{\mathcal{E}}_{\ell})\leq\frac{1}{m}\sum_{\mu}\overline{\lambda}(\mathcal{E}_{\ell}^{\mu})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>m</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>μ</mi></munder><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>μ</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{\lambda}(\overline{\mathcal{E}}_{\ell})\leq\frac{1}{m}\sum_{\mu}\overline{\lambda}(\mathcal{E}_{\ell}^{\mu}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem13.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem13.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">Further, recall that <math id="Thmtheorem13.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{\lambda}(\mathcal{E}_{0}^{\mu})=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>μ</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{\lambda}(\mathcal{E}_{0}^{\mu})=1</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="Thmtheorem13.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu,</annotation></semantics></math> and we set <math id="Thmtheorem13.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta_{\ell}^{\mu}=(\overline{\lambda}_{\ell}^{\mu})^{-1}/3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>η</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>μ</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>μ</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta_{\ell}^{\mu}=(\overline{\lambda}_{\ell}^{\mu})^{-1}/3</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus, each of these <math id="Thmtheorem13.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{\lambda}_{\ell}^{\mu}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>μ</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{\lambda}_{\ell}^{\mu}</annotation></semantics></math>s are infact identical (and equal to <math id="Thmtheorem13.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(4/9)^{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>9</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(4/9)^{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math>). Thus,</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex106" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex106.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\forall\mu,\overline{\lambda}(\overline{\mathcal{E}}_{\ell})\leq\overline{\lambda}^{\mu}_{\ell}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>μ</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\forall\mu,\overline{\lambda}(\overline{\mathcal{E}}_{\ell})\leq\overline{\lambda}^{\mu}_{\ell}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem13.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmtheorem13.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem13.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">Now, let <math id="Thmtheorem13.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P^{\mu}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>P</mi><mi>μ</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P^{\mu}</annotation></semantics></math> be the projection onto the column space of <math id="Thmtheorem13.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{\mu}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>μ</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{\mu}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then we note that for any vector <math id="Thmtheorem13.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex107" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex107.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v^{\top}\mathcal{E}^{\mu}_{\ell}v=(P^{\mu}v)^{\top}\mathcal{E}^{\mu}_{\ell}(P^{\mu}v)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>μ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>P</mi><mi>μ</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>μ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>P</mi><mi>μ</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v^{\top}\mathcal{E}^{\mu}_{\ell}v=(P^{\mu}v)^{\top}\mathcal{E}^{\mu}_{\ell}(P^{\mu}v).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem13.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem13.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">Indeed, any component in <math id="Thmtheorem13.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> orthogonal to the column space must lie in the kernel of <math id="Thmtheorem13.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}^{\mu}_{0}=A^{\mu}A^{\mu,\top}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>μ</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>μ</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em">⊤</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}^{\mu}_{0}=A^{\mu}A^{\mu,\top},</annotation></semantics></math> and we know that this kernel is invariant across the iterations. Further, note that since <math id="Thmtheorem13.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P^{\mu}v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>P</mi><mi>μ</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P^{\mu}v</annotation></semantics></math> lies in this column space, it is orthogonal to any eigenvector of <math id="Thmtheorem13.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}^{\mu}_{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>μ</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}^{\mu}_{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math> with zero eigenvalue, and so we can then conclude that</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex108" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex108.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(P^{\mu}v)^{\top}\mathcal{E}^{\mu}_{\ell}(P^{\mu}v)\geq\underline{\lambda}^{\mu}_{\ell}\|P^{\mu}v\|_{2}^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>P</mi><mi>μ</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>μ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>P</mi><mi>μ</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msubsup><munder accentunder="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>μ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>P</mi><mi>μ</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(P^{\mu}v)^{\top}\mathcal{E}^{\mu}_{\ell}(P^{\mu}v)\geq\underline{\lambda}^{\mu}_{\ell}\|P^{\mu}v\|_{2}^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem13.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmtheorem13.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem13.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">But then, if <math id="Thmtheorem13.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell\geq L(\varepsilon)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell\geq L(\varepsilon),</annotation></semantics></math> then for any unit vector <math id="Thmtheorem13.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math>, we have (for any <math id="Thmtheorem13.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math> in the last inequalities) that</span></p>
<table id="A5.EGx12" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.Ex109"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex109.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle v^{\top}\overline{\mathcal{E}}_{\ell}v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle v^{\top}\overline{\mathcal{E}}_{\ell}v</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex109.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{m}\sum_{\mu}v^{\top}\overline{\mathcal{E}}_{\ell}^{\mu}v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>m</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>μ</mi></munder></mstyle><mrow><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>μ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{m}\sum_{\mu}v^{\top}\overline{\mathcal{E}}_{\ell}^{\mu}v</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex110"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex110.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geq\frac{1}{m}\sum_{\mu}\underline{\lambda}_{\ell}^{\mu}\|P^{\mu}v\|_{2}^{2}=\frac{1}{m}\sum_{\mu}\frac{\overline{\lambda}_{\ell}^{\mu}}{(1+\kappa_{\ell}^{\mu})}\|P^{\mu}v\|_{2}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>m</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>μ</mi></munder></mstyle><mrow><msubsup><munder accentunder="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>μ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>P</mi><mi>μ</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>m</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>μ</mi></munder></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>μ</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>κ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>μ</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>P</mi><mi>μ</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq\frac{1}{m}\sum_{\mu}\underline{\lambda}_{\ell}^{\mu}\|P^{\mu}v\|_{2}^{2}=\frac{1}{m}\sum_{\mu}\frac{\overline{\lambda}_{\ell}^{\mu}}{(1+\kappa_{\ell}^{\mu})}\|P^{\mu}v\|_{2}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex111"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex111.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geq\frac{\overline{\lambda}_{\ell}^{\mu}}{1+\varepsilon}\frac{1}{m}\sum_{\mu}\|P^{\mu}v\|_{2}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>μ</mi></msubsup><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>m</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>μ</mi></munder></mstyle><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>P</mi><mi>μ</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq\frac{\overline{\lambda}_{\ell}^{\mu}}{1+\varepsilon}\frac{1}{m}\sum_{\mu}\|P^{\mu}v\|_{2}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex112"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex112.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geq\frac{\overline{\lambda}_{\ell}^{\mu}}{1+\varepsilon}\cdot\alpha," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>μ</mi></msubsup><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq\frac{\overline{\lambda}_{\ell}^{\mu}}{1+\varepsilon}\cdot\alpha,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem13.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem13.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">where we used the equality of the <math id="Thmtheorem13.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{\lambda}_{\ell}^{\mu}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>μ</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{\lambda}_{\ell}^{\mu},</annotation></semantics></math> the fact that <math id="Thmtheorem13.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa_{\ell}^{\mu}\leq 1+\varepsilon," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>κ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>μ</mi></msubsup><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa_{\ell}^{\mu}\leq 1+\varepsilon,</annotation></semantics></math> and finally the definition of <math id="Thmtheorem13.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>. Since <math id="Thmtheorem13.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> is a unit vector, we conclude that any Rayleigh quotient of <math id="Thmtheorem13.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{\mathcal{E}}_{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{\mathcal{E}}_{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math> is so lower bound, ergo</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex113" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex113.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\forall\mu,\underline{\lambda}(\overline{\mathcal{E}}_{\ell})\geq\frac{\overline{\lambda}_{\ell}^{\mu}}{1+\varepsilon}\cdot\alpha." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><munder accentunder="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mfrac><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>μ</mi></msubsup><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\forall\mu,\underline{\lambda}(\overline{\mathcal{E}}_{\ell})\geq\frac{\overline{\lambda}_{\ell}^{\mu}}{1+\varepsilon}\cdot\alpha.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem13.p4.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem13.p4.3.1" class="ltx_text">Putting this together with the upper bound on <math id="Thmtheorem13.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{\lambda}(\overline{\mathcal{E}}_{\ell})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{\lambda}(\overline{\mathcal{E}}_{\ell})</annotation></semantics></math>, we immediately conclude that</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex114" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex114.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{\kappa}_{\ell}\leq\frac{1+\varepsilon}{\alpha}.\qed" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>κ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mi>α</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">.</mo><mo class="ltx_mathvariant_italic" lspace="0.0835em" mathvariant="italic" separator="true">∎</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{\kappa}_{\ell}\leq\frac{1+\varepsilon}{\alpha}.\qed</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS2.p13" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS2.p13.1" class="ltx_p">At a high level, <math id="A5.SS2.p13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>α</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math> is the limiting condition number of the <math id="A5.SS2.p13.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{\mathcal{E}}_{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{\mathcal{E}}_{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math>s, where deviation from perfect conditioning occurs only due to how the various <math id="A5.SS2.p13.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}^{\mu}_{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>μ</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}^{\mu}_{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math> energise distinct subspaces for large <math id="A5.SS2.p13.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math>. We note that this dependence is tight—if all the <math id="A5.SS2.p13.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}^{\mu}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>μ</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}^{\mu}</annotation></semantics></math> share the top eigenvector, then the upper bound on <math id="A5.SS2.p13.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{\lambda}(\overline{\mathcal{E}}_{\ell})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{\lambda}(\overline{\mathcal{E}}_{\ell})</annotation></semantics></math> is exact, while the lowest nonzero eigenvector of <math id="A5.SS2.p13.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{\mathcal{E}}_{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{\mathcal{E}}_{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math> is precisely the direction that achieves the minimum in the definition of the diversity index.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS2.p14" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS2.p14.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="A5.SS2.p14.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_bold ltx_font_italic">Concluding the argument.</em> With this in hand, we can argue the decay of <math id="A5.SS2.p14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{\ell}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{\ell},</annotation></semantics></math> and so attain error control.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 2. ‣ 5.2 Distributed setting ‣ 5 Evaluation of EAGLE ‣ Linear Transformers Implicitly DiscoverUnified Numerical Algorithms" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="A5.SS2.p15" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS2.p15.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.p15.1.1" class="ltx_text">Recall that <math id="A5.SS2.p15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D-\hat{D}_{\ell}=W_{*}N_{\ell}C_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>D</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D-\hat{D}_{\ell}=W_{*}N_{\ell}C_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>. We again assume that <math id="A5.SS2.p15.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{\lambda}^{\mu}_{0}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mn>0</mn><mi>μ</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{\lambda}^{\mu}_{0}=1</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A5.SS2.p15.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu,</annotation></semantics></math> and that <math id="A5.SS2.p15.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta_{\ell}^{\mu}=(\overline{\lambda}^{\mu}_{\ell})^{-1}/3." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>η</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>μ</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>μ</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta_{\ell}^{\mu}=(\overline{\lambda}^{\mu}_{\ell})^{-1}/3.</annotation></semantics></math> We set <math id="A5.SS2.p15.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{\ell}=(\overline{\lambda}^{\mu}_{\ell})^{-1}\leq\overline{\lambda}(\overline{\mathcal{E}}_{\ell})^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>μ</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{\ell}=(\overline{\lambda}^{\mu}_{\ell})^{-1}\leq\overline{\lambda}(\overline{\mathcal{E}}_{\ell})^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then, as before, we have (restricted to the appropriate subspace if <math id="A5.SS2.p15.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{\mathcal{E}}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{\mathcal{E}}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> is not full rank)</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex115" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex115.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\|I-\eta_{\ell}\overline{\mathcal{E}}_{\ell}\|_{2}\leq(1-1/\overline{\kappa}_{\ell})\leq\exp(-1/\overline{\kappa}_{\ell})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.0835em">≤</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>κ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>κ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|I-\eta_{\ell}\overline{\mathcal{E}}_{\ell}\|_{2}\leq(1-1/\overline{\kappa}_{\ell})\leq\exp(-1/\overline{\kappa}_{\ell}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.p15.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.p15.2.1" class="ltx_text">By Lemma <a href="#Thmtheorem13" title="Lemma 13. ‣ E.2 Distributed Analysis ‣ Appendix E Theoretical Analyses ‣ Linear Transformers Implicitly DiscoverUnified Numerical Algorithms" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">13</span></a>, for <math id="A5.SS2.p15.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell\geq L(1)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell\geq L(1),</annotation></semantics></math> we have <math id="A5.SS2.p15.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{\kappa}_{\ell}\leq 2/\alpha," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>κ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{\kappa}_{\ell}\leq 2/\alpha,</annotation></semantics></math> and so</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex116" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex116.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\|N_{\ell}\|\leq\exp(-\sum_{l=L(1)}^{\ell}1/\overline{\kappa}_{\ell})\leq\exp(-\alpha(\ell-L(1))/2)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><mo lspace="0.0835em">≤</mo><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.055em">−</mo><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></munderover><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>κ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>α</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>L</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|N_{\ell}\|\leq\exp(-\sum_{l=L(1)}^{\ell}1/\overline{\kappa}_{\ell})\leq\exp(-\alpha(\ell-L(1))/2),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.p15.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.p15.3.1" class="ltx_text">which is smaller than <math id="A5.SS2.p15.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\iota\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ι</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\iota\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math> if</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex117" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex117.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell\geq L(1)+\frac{2}{\alpha}\log\frac{1}{\iota\varepsilon}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mi>α</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>ι</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell\geq L(1)+\frac{2}{\alpha}\log\frac{1}{\iota\varepsilon}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.p15.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.p15.4.1" class="ltx_text">Of course, <math id="A5.SS2.p15.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L(1)=3+\lceil 3/5\log(\max_{\mu}\kappa^{\mu}_{0})\rceil," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌈</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msubsup><mi>κ</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>μ</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌉</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L(1)=3+\lceil 3/5\log(\max_{\mu}\kappa^{\mu}_{0})\rceil,</annotation></semantics></math> and setting <math id="A5.SS2.p15.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\iota" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ι</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\iota</annotation></semantics></math> so small that error to <math id="A5.SS2.p15.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ε</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math> follows in the same way as the proof of Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 1. ‣ 5.1 Unconstrained (centralized) setting ‣ 5 Evaluation of EAGLE ‣ Linear Transformers Implicitly DiscoverUnified Numerical Algorithms" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> concludes the argument.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS2.p16" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS2.p16.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="A5.SS2.p16.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_bold ltx_font_italic">Comment on Rates</em><span id="A5.SS2.p16.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span> We note that, in the distributed setting, within-machine computation is typically much cheaper than across-machine communication. As a result, the protocol we have analyzed above, wherein each machine begins with the same value of <math id="A5.SS2.p16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{\lambda}^{\mu}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mn>0</mn><mi>μ</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{\lambda}^{\mu}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>, is cheap to follow by using power-iteration at each machine. Given this choice, the value <math id="A5.SS2.p16.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{\lambda}^{\mu}_{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>μ</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{\lambda}^{\mu}_{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math> is simply equal to <math id="A5.SS2.p16.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(4/9)^{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>9</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(4/9)^{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math> for every machine, and setting the learning rate <math id="A5.SS2.p16.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta_{\ell}^{\mu}=\rho_{\ell}^{\mu}/3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>η</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>μ</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>ρ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>μ</mi></msubsup><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta_{\ell}^{\mu}=\rho_{\ell}^{\mu}/3</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A5.SS2.p16.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{\ell}^{\mu}=(9/4)^{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>ρ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>μ</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>9</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{\ell}^{\mu}=(9/4)^{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math> is trivial, and does not require any communication. We also note that setting <math id="A5.SS2.p16.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{\ell}=\rho_{\ell}^{\mu}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>ρ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>μ</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{\ell}=\rho_{\ell}^{\mu}</annotation></semantics></math> in each machine, and then averaging the results of the updates together is sufficient, since <math id="A5.SS2.p16.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{\ell}^{\mu}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>ρ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>μ</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{\ell}^{\mu}</annotation></semantics></math> is constant across all machines. Thus, we recover exactly the structure presented in Algorithm <a href="#algofigure1" title="List of algofigures 1 ‣ 4 Emergent Algorithm ‣ Linear Transformers Implicitly DiscoverUnified Numerical Algorithms" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, with <math id="A5.SS2.p16.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma=1,\eta=1/3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma=1,\eta=1/3</annotation></semantics></math>. Note, again, that for the sake of stability, instead of working with decaying <math id="A5.SS2.p16.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math> and exploding <math id="A5.SS2.p16.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta_{\ell},\gamma_{\ell}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta_{\ell},\gamma_{\ell},</annotation></semantics></math> we can again rescale each <math id="A5.SS2.p16.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{\ell}^{\mu},B_{\ell}^{\mu}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>μ</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>μ</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{\ell}^{\mu},B_{\ell}^{\mu}</annotation></semantics></math> by <math id="A5.SS2.p16.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3/2</annotation></semantics></math> after updates.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS2.p17" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS2.p17.1" class="ltx_p">In general, if this normalisation is not carried out, the machines may actually set their values for <math id="A5.SS2.p17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math> as distinct <math id="A5.SS2.p17.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{\ell}^{\mu}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>μ</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{\ell}^{\mu}</annotation></semantics></math>s. The net effect would be that we need to analyze a slightly different version of <math id="A5.SS2.p17.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{\mathcal{E}}_{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{\mathcal{E}}_{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math> that is sensitive to inter-machine variations in <math id="A5.SS2.p17.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{\ell}^{\mu}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>μ</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{\ell}^{\mu},</annotation></semantics></math> which in turn would rely on how strongly <math id="A5.SS2.p17.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{\lambda}^{\mu}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mn>0</mn><mi>μ</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{\lambda}^{\mu}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> varies across machines. We leave the study of such scenarios to future work.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
</article>
</div>
</div>
